const KANT_GLOSSARY_EXAMPLES = {"erkenntnis":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:630","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-016.12","de":"Eine genaue Erkenntniß ist eine solche, die mit dem Gegenstand in allen Stücken uebereinstimmt, und dem Zweck gemäß ist.","d":[12,22],"en":"An exact cognition is one that agrees with the object in all respects and is in accordance with the end.","e":[9,18]}],"kenntnis":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:107","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-019.0","de":"Die absoluten Kenntnißen von denen Dingen aber sind weit schwerer, als die Erkenntniße, die man sich durch Vergleichungen erwirbet.","d":[14,24],"en":"But absolute acquaintance with things is far more difficult than the cognitions one acquires through comparisons.","e":[13,25]}],"wissen":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:639","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-009.7","de":"Der Grund des führwahrhaltens durch den Glauben ist oft hinreichender, als das Wißen.","d":[79,84],"en":"The ground of holding-to-be-true through believing is often more sufficient than knowing.","e":[81,88]}],"wissenschaft":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:298","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s17-008.0","de":"Die Frantzosen sind sonderlich von dem caractère, daß bey ihnen die Wißenschaften mehr extensive, als intensive wachßen.","d":[68,81],"en":"The French are especially of the caractère that among them the sciences grow more extensive than intensive.","e":[63,71]}],"vorstellung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:119","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-122.1","de":"Eine Vorstellung aber ist dunckel (um zu unserer Materie zurück zu kehren) der man sich unmittelbahr nichtbewust ist.","d":[5,16],"en":"But a representation is obscure (to return to our matter) of which one is not immediately conscious.","e":[6,20]}],"begriff":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:139","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-326.0","de":"Die Ausführlichkeit bestehet eigentlich in nichts anders als darinn, daß nichts fehlet, daß der Begriff gantz seyn kann.","d":[96,103],"en":"Exhaustiveness consists properly in nothing other than that nothing is lacking, that the concept can be whole.","e":[89,96]}],"anschauung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:129","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-209.0","de":"Sinnliche Klarheit ist nichts anders als die Lebhaftigkeit, in der Anschauung ist die Klarheit aber die sinnliche Klarheit.","d":[67,77],"en":"Sensible clarity is nothing other than vividness; in intuition, however, clarity is sensible clarity.","e":[53,62]}],"idee":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:648","link":"busolt:busolt-s16-002.1","de":"Auch nicht jedes Können ist eine Kunst denn diese ist das Vermögen, etwas nach Ideen herauszubringen.","d":[79,84],"en":"Nor is every being-able an art, for this is the faculty of bringing something forth according to ideas.","e":[97,102]}],"ideal":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:47","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-045.2","de":"Das urbild aller Vollkommenheiten aber ist immer nur in Gedancken. es ist ein Archetypon, und blos ein Ideal.","d":[103,108],"en":"The archetype of all perfections, however, is always only in thought. It is an archetypon, and merely an ideal.","e":[105,110]}],"erfahrung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:18","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-025.1","de":"Allein wenn keine andere Principia als die Erfahrungen sind . so bleibt eine gesunde Vernunft doch eine gemeine Vernunft.","d":[43,54],"en":"But if there are no other principia than experiences, a sound reason still remains a common reason.","e":[41,52]}],"wahrnehmung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.7","de":"Weil aber aus lauter besondern Säzzen nichts folgt; so ist der Verstand bemüht durch seine Wahrnehmungen hier Regeln d.i. allgemeine Säzze zu machen.","d":[91,104],"en":"But because nothing follows from purely particular propositions, the understanding is concerned to make rules here through its perceptions, i.e. universal propositions.","e":[127,138]}],"empfindung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:619","link":"busolt:busolt-s05-030.5","de":"Empfindungen ueberraschen, Erkenntniß kommt nach und nach; jene sind etwas vorübergehendes, diese etwas Beständiges.","d":[0,12],"en":"Sensations take one by surprise, cognition comes gradually; those are something transitory, this something lasting.","e":[0,10]}],"erscheinung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:102","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-221.0","de":"Es ist gleichsahm eine gantz ungewöhnliche, unnatürliche Erscheinung, die denen Gesetzen des Verstandes wiederspricht.","d":[57,68],"en":"It is, as it were, a wholly unusual, unnatural appearance, which contradicts the laws of the understanding.","e":[47,57]}],"phaenomenon":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:102","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-220.0","de":"Ein jeder Irrthum ist ein Phaenomenon, ein Rätzel in absicht des Begriffs von der Möglichkeit desselben.","d":[26,37],"en":"Every error is a phenomenon, a riddle with respect to the concept of the possibility of it.","e":[17,27]}],"gegenstand":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:630","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-016.12","de":"Eine genaue Erkenntniß ist eine solche, die mit dem Gegenstand in allen Stücken uebereinstimmt, und dem Zweck gemäß ist.","d":[52,62],"en":"An exact cognition is one that agrees with the object in all respects and is in accordance with the end.","e":[47,53]}],"objekt":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:72","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-051.0","de":"Eine Erkenntniß, die Extensive groß ist, oder die sehr viele Objecten in sich begreift, nennet der Autor eine Polyhistorie.","d":[61,69],"en":"A cognition that is extensively great, or that comprehends very many objects within itself, the author calls a polyhistory.","e":[69,76]}],"subjekt":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 302","link":"meier:meier-para-302.2","de":"Ein allgemein verneinendes Urtheil ist wahr, wenn das Prädicat allen unter dem Subjecte enthaltenen zuwider ist §.301.","d":[79,87],"en":"A universal negative judgment is true if the predicate is repugnant to all those contained under the subject §.301.","e":[101,108]}],"merkmal":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-080.0","de":"Wenn die Merckmahle nicht weniger enthalten, als zur unterscheidung der Sache nöthig ist, so ist dieses eine Praecision.","d":[9,19],"en":"If the marks contain no less than is necessary for the distinction of the thing, then this is a precision.","e":[7,12]}],"kennzeichen":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:268","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-060.1","de":"Das dencke ich zwar bey dem Begrife des Saltzes, es sind doch aber nicht alle mögliche Kennzeichen des Saltzes selbst.","d":[87,98],"en":"I do indeed think that in the concept of salt, but these are not all possible criteria of salt itself.","e":[78,86]}],"kriterium":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-001.8","de":"Das allgemeine Kriterium der Wahrheit ist hier also bloß Formale, die Uebereinstimmung des Erkenntnißes mit dem obiect.","d":[15,24],"en":"The universal criterion of truth is here, then, merely formal, the agreement of cognition with the object.","e":[14,23]}],"inbegriff":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:649","link":"busolt:busolt-s16-005.14","de":"Der Inbegriff der Erkentniß ist entweder ein aggregat oder ein System; diese Erkentniße mögen historische oder vernunft Erkentniße seyn.","d":[4,13],"en":"The sum total of cognition is either an aggregate or a system; these cognitions may be historical cognitions or cognitions of reason.","e":[4,13]}],"gelehrte-erkenntnis":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 130","link":"meier:meier-para-130.1","de":"Es ist demnach nicht eine jede dunkele Erkenntniss falsch; 2) ist keine gelehrte Erkenntniss, in so fern sie dunkel ist.","d":[72,92],"en":"Not every obscure cognition is therefore false; 2) is no learned cognition, insofar as it is obscure.","e":[57,74]}],"gelehrsamkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:20","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-032.9","de":"Die Logic, die ein Organon der rationalen Gelahrtsamkeit ist, geht nicht auf Historische, sonderen rationalische Erkenntniße.","d":[42,56],"en":"The logic that is an organon of rational erudition does not concern historical but rational cognitions.","e":[41,50]}],"gelehrter":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-002.3","de":"Hingegen ist unter einem schlechten Kleide oft ein Gelehrter verborgen, eben so ist es mit den Erkenntnißen.","d":[51,60],"en":"On the other hand, a scholar is often hidden beneath a poor garment; it is just so with cognitions.","e":[21,28]}],"weitlaeufigkeit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 264","link":"meier:meier-para-264.1","de":"Denn je abstracter sie ist, desto weniger enthält sie in sich §.259, und desto leichter kann sie also ohne viele Verwirrung durchdacht werden; 2) die Weitläuftigkeit der Erkenntniss §.263.","d":[150,165],"en":"For the more abstract it is, the less it contains in itself §.259, and the more easily it can therefore be thought through without much confusion; 2) the extensiveness of cognition §.263.","e":[154,167]}],"armseligkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:66","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-001.0","de":"Die Weitläufigkeit der gelahrten Erkenntniß wird der Armseeligkeit derselben entgegen gesezt.","d":[53,66],"en":"The extensiveness of learned cognition is opposed to its paltriness.","e":[57,67]}],"groesse":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 301","link":"meier:meier-para-301.8","de":"In so ferne ein Urtheil entweder ein einzelnes oder ein gemeines ist, in so ferne schreibt man ihm eine Grösse zu (quantitas iudicii).","d":[104,110],"en":"Insofar as a judgment is either a singular or a common one, insofar one ascribes to it a magnitude (quantitas iudicii).","e":[89,98]}],"wahrheit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-001.8","de":"Das allgemeine Kriterium der Wahrheit ist hier also bloß Formale, die Uebereinstimmung des Erkenntnißes mit dem obiect.","d":[29,37],"en":"The universal criterion of truth is here, then, merely formal, the agreement of cognition with the object.","e":[27,32]}],"falschheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:233","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-622.10","de":"Ferner ist auch die Falschheit der Form noch weit ausgebreiteter, und allgemeiner, als die Falschheit der Materie.","d":[20,30],"en":"Furthermore, the falsity of the form is also far more widespread and more universal than the falsity of the matter.","e":[17,24]}],"irrtum":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:633","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-022.28","de":"Wenn ich aber etwas urteilen muß z.E. In den Dingen der Religion, so ist in diesem Fall zuweilen ein Irrthum unvermeidlich.","d":[101,108],"en":"But if I must judge something, e.g. in the things of religion, then in this case an error is at times unavoidable.","e":[84,89]}],"unwissenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:110","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-041.0","de":"Außer der Unwißenheit giebt es ein anderes noch gefährlicheres Übel im Verstande, und dieses ist der Irrthum.","d":[10,21],"en":"Besides ignorance there is another, still more dangerous evil in the understanding, and this is error.","e":[8,17]}],"schein":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:640","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-018.3","de":"Es ist aber fehlerhaft, wenn man ein Vorläufiges Urtheil für ein bestimmtes hält denn der Schein kann trügen.","d":[90,96],"en":"But it is faulty if one takes a provisional judgment for a determinate one, for semblance can deceive.","e":[80,89]}],"klarheit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 133","link":"meier:meier-para-133.4","de":"Unterdessen ist eine Erkenntniss um so viel vollkommener, je mehr sich ihre Klarheit der gänzlichen Klarheit nähert§.124.","d":[76,84],"en":"Meanwhile a cognition is all the more perfect, the more its clarity approaches total clarity §.124.","e":[60,67]}],"dunkelheit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 125","link":"meier:meier-para-125.4","de":"Und als dennist entweder der Gegenstand vornehmlich an dieser Dunkelheit schuld, oder der Mensch, dem die Erkenntniss dunkel ist.","d":[62,72],"en":"And then either the object is chiefly to blame for this obscurity, or the human being to whom the cognition is obscure.","e":[56,65]}],"deutlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-346.1","de":"Ein höherer Grad der Deutlichkeit der Erkenntniß hingegen durch Coordinirte Merckmahle ist die ausgebreitete Deutlichkeit.","d":[21,33],"en":"A higher degree of distinctness of cognition through coordinated marks, on the other hand, is extensive distinctness.","e":[19,31]}],"verworrenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:41","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-008.1","de":"Verworrenheit, und Deutlichkeit finden also nur bey zusammen gesezten Erkenntnißen statt.","d":[0,13],"en":"Confusedness and distinctness therefore occur only in composite cognitions.","e":[0,12]}],"ausfuehrlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:139","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-326.0","de":"Die Ausführlichkeit bestehet eigentlich in nichts anders als darinn, daß nichts fehlet, daß der Begriff gantz seyn kann.","d":[4,19],"en":"Exhaustiveness consists properly in nothing other than that nothing is lacking, that the concept can be whole.","e":[0,14]}],"vollstaendigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:138","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-315.0","de":"Die Vollständigkeit selbst aber bestehet in nichts anders als in der Completudine, und in der Praecision.","d":[4,19],"en":"Completeness itself, however, consists in nothing other than in Completudine and in precision.","e":[0,12]}],"praezision":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-080.0","de":"Wenn die Merckmahle nicht weniger enthalten, als zur unterscheidung der Sache nöthig ist, so ist dieses eine Praecision.","d":[109,119],"en":"If the marks contain no less than is necessary for the distinction of the thing, then this is a precision.","e":[96,105]}],"gruendlichkeit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:637","link":"busolt:busolt-s13-001.2","de":"Profunditas oder Gründlichkeit ist die Reihe der Subordinirten Merkmahle, oder den Merkmalen von den Merkmahlen.","d":[17,30],"en":"Profunditas or thoroughness is the series of the subordinated marks, or of the marks of the marks.","e":[15,27]}],"lebhaftigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:129","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-209.0","de":"Sinnliche Klarheit ist nichts anders als die Lebhaftigkeit, in der Anschauung ist die Klarheit aber die sinnliche Klarheit.","d":[45,58],"en":"Sensible clarity is nothing other than vividness; in intuition, however, clarity is sensible clarity.","e":[39,48]}],"gewissheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:225","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-576.0","de":"Von der apodictischen Gewisheit ist noch verschieden die mathematische gewisheit in der Anschauung, die evident ist.","d":[22,31],"en":"Different still from apodictic certainty is mathematical certainty in intuition, which is evident.","e":[31,40]}],"ungewissheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:205","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-459.0","de":"In einem inneren Beweise ist man sich unmittelbahr bewust der Ungewisheit in einer Erkenntniß.","d":[62,73],"en":"In an inner proof one is immediately aware of the uncertainty in a cognition.","e":[50,61]}],"wahrscheinlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:143","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-014.1","de":"Das Urtheil nach dem Maaße der Wahrscheinlichkeit ist keine Überredung sonderen das Urtheil aus der blosen Scheinbahrkeit.","d":[31,49],"en":"Judgment according to the measure of probability is not persuasion but judgment from mere plausibility.","e":[37,48]}],"scheinbarkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:143","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-014.1","de":"Das Urtheil nach dem Maaße der Wahrscheinlichkeit ist keine Überredung sonderen das Urtheil aus der blosen Scheinbahrkeit.","d":[107,121],"en":"Judgment according to the measure of probability is not persuasion but judgment from mere plausibility.","e":[90,102]}],"vollkommenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-342.0","de":"Bey schönen d.i. aesthetischen Erkenntnißen aber dagegen ist die Praecision wiederum eine entbehrliche Vollkommenheit.","d":[103,117],"en":"In beautiful, i.e., aesthetic cognitions, on the other hand, precision is in turn a dispensable perfection.","e":[96,106]}],"unvollkommenheit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 23","link":"meier:meier-para-23.1","de":"Die Unvollkommenheiten der Erkenntniss finden entweder in ihr statt, in so ferne sie deutlich, oder in so ferne sie undeutlich ist §.14.","d":[4,22],"en":"The imperfections of cognition occur either in it insofar as it is distinct, or insofar as it is indistinct §.14.","e":[4,17]}],"mangel":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:642","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-027.0","de":"Uebereilung ist ein Mangel der Ueberlegung des Verstandes Vorurtheil geschieht durch einen Hang nicht durch Uebereilung.","d":[20,26],"en":"Precipitancy is a lack of the reflection of the understanding; prejudice happens through a propensity, not through precipitancy.","e":[18,22]}],"horizont":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:68","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-021.4","de":"Der logische Horizont in Ansehung unserer Fähigkeiten ist 1.) Historisch der der weitläufigste ist, und seyn muß.","d":[13,21],"en":"The logical horizon with regard to our capacities is 1.) historical, which is the most extensive, and must be.","e":[12,19]}],"wichtigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:112","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-050.1","de":"Alle Wichtigkeit der Erkenntniß aber bestehet nur alsdenn, wenn sie allein vor sich ohne Vergleich mit anderen Erkenntnißen betrachtet wird.","d":[5,16],"en":"But all importance of cognition exists only when it is considered by itself alone, without comparison with other cognitions.","e":[8,18]}],"fruchtbarkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:50","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-060.0","de":"Die Theoretische Vollkommenheit gehet eigentlich auf die Quantitaet derselben, als z.E. die Weitlaufigkeit, Fruchtbahrkeit.","d":[108,122],"en":"Theoretical perfection goes properly to the quantity of it, as, e.g., extensiveness, fruitfulness.","e":[85,97]}],"brauchbarkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:19","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-029.5","de":"Der gemeine und gesunde Verstand ist ein kleiner, aber richtiger Verstand, und seine Erkenntniß hat eine große Brauchbahrkeit. in einem Land-Striche von Bauren finden sich Lang nicht so viele Irrthümeren, alß in einem Bezirk von gelahrten, der eben so groß ist.","d":[111,125],"en":"The common and sound understanding is a small but correct understanding, and its cognition has great usefulness. In a stretch of country of peasants far fewer errors are found than in a district of scholars of equal size.","e":[101,111]}],"fuerwahrhalten":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:229","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-602.0","de":"Bey der gewisheit ist nicht die wahrheit selbst der Sache, die wir erkennen, sonderen das Vorwahrhalten derselben nöthig.","d":[90,103],"en":"In certainty, what is needed is not the truth itself of the thing that we cognize, but the holding-to-be-true of it.","e":[91,109]}],"meinen":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:638","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-008.1","de":"Meinen ist weder ein Subiectiuer noch obiectiuer, Glauben nur ein Subiectiuer Zureichender Grund des führwahrhaltens.","d":[0,6],"en":"Opining is neither a subjective nor an objective, believing only a subjective sufficient ground of holding-to-be-true.","e":[0,7]}],"meinung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:218","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-528.0","de":"In diesem Paragrapho redet der Autor von einer Meinung überhaupt. sie ist aber der Überredung contradistinguiret.","d":[47,54],"en":"In this paragraph the author speaks of an opinion in general. It is, however, contradistinguished from persuasion.","e":[42,49]}],"glaube":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 214","link":"meier:meier-para-214.1","de":"Der vernünfti ge  oder sehende Glaube (fides oculata, rationalis) ist die Fertigkeit nur glaubwürdigen Zeugen zu glauben.","d":[31,37],"en":"Reasonable or seeing belief (fides oculata, rationalis) is the habit of believing only credible witnesses.","e":[21,27]}],"ueberzeugung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:218","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-529.0","de":"Der Unterschied der Überredung von der Überzeugung aber ist ziemlich schwer, und wird also sehr selten recht bestimmet.","d":[39,50],"en":"The difference between persuasion and conviction, however, is rather difficult, and is therefore very seldom properly determined.","e":[38,48]}],"ueberredung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:218","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-529.0","de":"Der Unterschied der Überredung von der Überzeugung aber ist ziemlich schwer, und wird also sehr selten recht bestimmet.","d":[20,30],"en":"The difference between persuasion and conviction, however, is rather difficult, and is therefore very seldom properly determined.","e":[23,33]}],"beifall":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 206","link":"meier:meier-para-206.3","de":"Der Glaube (fides, fides historica) ist der Beifall, den wir einer Sache um eines Zeugnisses willen geben.","d":[44,51],"en":"Belief (fides, fides historica) is the assent which we give to a thing on account of a testimony.","e":[39,45]}],"zweifel":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 176","link":"meier:meier-para-176.0","de":"Wenn wir etwas für wahr oder für falsch halten, so nennet man eine jedwede Erkenntniss eines Grundes zum Gegentheil, einen Zweifel (dubium).","d":[123,130],"en":"When we hold something to be true or false, any cognition of a ground for the opposite is called a doubt (dubium).","e":[99,104]}],"vorurteil":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:642","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-027.0","de":"Uebereilung ist ein Mangel der Ueberlegung des Verstandes Vorurtheil geschieht durch einen Hang nicht durch Uebereilung.","d":[58,68],"en":"Precipitancy is a lack of the reflection of the understanding; prejudice happens through a propensity, not through precipitancy.","e":[63,72]}],"zeugnis":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 208","link":"meier:meier-para-208.1","de":"Ein Hörerzeuge (testis auritus) ist kein Augenzeuge, sondern er hat nur das Zeugniss anderer von der Sache erfahren.","d":[76,84],"en":"A hearsay witness (testis auritus) is no eyewitness, but has only learned of the thing from the testimony of others.","e":[96,105]}],"zeuge":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 214","link":"meier:meier-para-214.1","de":"Der vernünfti ge  oder sehende Glaube (fides oculata, rationalis) ist die Fertigkeit nur glaubwürdigen Zeugen zu glauben.","d":[103,109],"en":"Reasonable or seeing belief (fides oculata, rationalis) is the habit of believing only credible witnesses.","e":[96,105]}],"glaubwuerdigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:249","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-685.1","de":"Ein blinder glauben aber ist derjenige, der ein Zeugniß annimt, ohne Prüfung, und Untersuchung der Glaubwürdigkeit desselben.","d":[99,114],"en":"A blind belief, however, is that which accepts a testimony without examination and investigation of its credibility.","e":[104,115]}],"unglaube":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:249","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-683.5","de":"Diese Unglaubigkeit kann auch der logische Glaube genanndt werden, und ist also vom moralischen Unglauben sehr unterschieden.","d":[96,105],"en":"This incredulity can also be called logical belief, and is thus very different from moral unbelief.","e":[90,98]}],"skeptizismus":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:646","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-050.4","de":"Diese lezte sind Principien Skeptizismus streitet der Vernunft alle Gewißheit ab, und halt sie für ungewiß.","d":[28,40],"en":"These latter are principles. Skepticism denies all certainty to reason and holds it to be uncertain.","e":[29,39]}],"beobachtung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:151","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-089.0","de":"Durch Beobachtungen, Experimente, und eine häufige, auch öfters wiederholte Erfahrung erlanget man eine Gewisheit der Sinne.","d":[6,19],"en":"Through observations, experiments, and frequent, often repeated experience one attains a certainty of the senses.","e":[8,20]}],"versuch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:224","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-565.1","de":"Ofters sind viele Versuche zu erdichten gantz umsonst, indem man dadurch keine wahrheit erfindet.","d":[18,26],"en":"Often many attempts at invention are quite in vain, in that one thereby discovers no truth.","e":[11,19]}],"hypothese":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:223","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-560.0","de":"Wir müßen also neue Gründe erdichten, und diese neue Gründe sind nichts anders, als die Hypotheses Subsidiariae.","d":[88,98],"en":"We must therefore invent new grounds, and these new grounds are nothing other than the hypotheses subsidiariae.","e":[87,97]}],"verstand":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:642","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-027.0","de":"Uebereilung ist ein Mangel der Ueberlegung des Verstandes Vorurtheil geschieht durch einen Hang nicht durch Uebereilung.","d":[47,57],"en":"Precipitancy is a lack of the reflection of the understanding; prejudice happens through a propensity, not through precipitancy.","e":[48,61]}],"vernunft":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:652","link":"busolt:busolt-s17-024.7","de":"Einen Vernunft Ungläubigen könnte man auch Moralisch ungläubig nennen: denn die Vernunft läuft zulezt auf Moralitaet aus.","d":[6,14],"en":"A rational unbeliever could also be called morally unbelieving: for reason ultimately runs out into morality.","e":[68,74]}],"urteilskraft":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:611","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-011.3","de":"Die aesthetic ist die Lehre der Sinnlichen Urtheilskraft, ob ein Werk des Genies, oder sonst etwas gefällt, oder nicht.","d":[43,56],"en":"Aesthetic is the doctrine of the sensible power of judgment, whether a work of genius, or something else, pleases or not.","e":[42,59]}],"sinnlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:127","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-190.1","de":"Die Sinnlichkeit ist die vollkommenheit der Erkenntniß, da wir uns eine Sache so wie Gegenstände der Sinne vorstellen.","d":[4,16],"en":"Sensibility is the perfection of cognition in which we represent a thing to ourselves as objects of the senses.","e":[0,11]}],"sinn":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:653","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-007.3","de":"Sinnliche Erkentniße a posteriori heißen empirische. conceptus sensitiui sind, wo das obiect durch die Sinne gegeben wird.","d":[103,108],"en":"Sensible cognitions a posteriori are called empirical. Conceptus sensitivi are where the object is given through the senses.","e":[117,123]}],"sinnlich":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:611","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-011.3","de":"Die aesthetic ist die Lehre der Sinnlichen Urtheilskraft, ob ein Werk des Genies, oder sonst etwas gefällt, oder nicht.","d":[32,42],"en":"Aesthetic is the doctrine of the sensible power of judgment, whether a work of genius, or something else, pleases or not.","e":[33,41]}],"einbildungskraft":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:617","link":"busolt:busolt-s05-024.0","de":"1.) Die aesthetische Vorstellung ist die Vorstellung durch die Sinne oder Einbildungskraft, diese imagination gehöret gleichsam mit zu den Sinnen, sie ist ihr copist, sie ist die Quelle der Anschauung.","d":[74,90],"en":"1.) The aesthetic representation is the representation through the senses or the imagination; this imagination belongs, as it were, with the senses, it is their copyist, it is the source of intuition.","e":[81,92]}],"einbildung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:203","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-445.0","de":"Die Arzte sind oftmals an der Feigheit ihrer Patienten selbst schuld, sie Speißen sie mehrentheils immer mit leeren Worten, und Bedingungen, Einbildungen.","d":[141,153],"en":"Physicians are often themselves to blame for the cowardice of their patients; they mostly feed them always with empty words, and conditions, imaginings.","e":[141,151]}],"gedaechtnis":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:74","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-066.1","de":"Diese kommen alle zur Geschichte zu, und diese Wißenschaft wird endlich also weitläuftig werden, und zunehmen, daß endlich unser Gedächtniß lange nicht groß genung seyn wird. da es jezt schon so schwer ist.","d":[129,139],"en":"These all come to history, and this science will finally become so extensive and increase so much that at last our memory will by far not be large enough, when it is already so difficult now.","e":[115,121]}],"witz":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:193","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-367.0","de":"Manchmal hilft ein Fehler den Witz, die Talente etc. eines Menschen, welche sonst nicht sehr Beträchtlich sind, dennoch hervorscheinen und schimmeren zu Laßen.","d":[30,34],"en":"Sometimes a fault helps the wit, the talents etc. of a person, which are otherwise not very considerable, nevertheless to shine forth and shimmer.","e":[28,31]}],"scharfsinn":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:613","link":"busolt:busolt-s03-001.0","de":"Aristoteles war der erste Logiker, er ist der Vater der Logic: Seine Logic ist ein Produkt von großem Scharfsinn.","d":[102,112],"en":"Aristotle was the first logician, he is the father of logic: His logic is a product of great acumen.","e":[93,99]}],"genie":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:611","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-011.3","de":"Die aesthetic ist die Lehre der Sinnlichen Urtheilskraft, ob ein Werk des Genies, oder sonst etwas gefällt, oder nicht.","d":[74,80],"en":"Aesthetic is the doctrine of the sensible power of judgment, whether a work of genius, or something else, pleases or not.","e":[79,85]}],"aufmerksamkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:96","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-149.2","de":"Das heißt in einer Erkenntniß grob, wozu nur eine kleine Aufmercksamkeit, das heißt subtil, zu deßen Klahrheit eine größere Aufmercksamkeit erforderet wird.","d":[57,72],"en":"That is called gross in a cognition for which only a little attention is needed; that is called subtle for whose clarity a greater attention is required.","e":[60,69]}],"abstraktion":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:262","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-038.7","de":"Absonderung, Abstraction, Trennung, Separation sind also von einander unterschieden.","d":[13,24],"en":"Absonderung, abstraction, Trennung, separation are thus distinguished from one another.","e":[13,24]}],"ueberlegung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:167","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-218.1","de":"Ein Vorurtheil aber ist nichts anders, als ein gewißer allgemeiner grund ohne alle Überlegung zu urtheilen.","d":[83,93],"en":"A prejudice, however, is nothing other than a certain general ground for judging without any reflection.","e":[93,103]}],"reflexion":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:130","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-220.0","de":"2 do Die logische Deutlichkeit hingegen nach Gesetzen des Verstandes, und der Vernunft, oder der Logic aber ist nichts anders, als die Deutlichkeit der Reflection","d":[152,162],"en":"2 do Logical distinctness, on the other hand, according to laws of the understanding and of reason, or of logic, is nothing other than the distinctness of reflection","e":[155,165]}],"bewusstsein":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 117","link":"meier:meier-para-117.3","de":"Obgleich beide Arten ein Bewusstsein verursachen können, so sind doch die bejahenden bessere Merkmale als die verneinenden.","d":[25,36],"en":"Although both kinds can cause consciousness, the affirmative are nevertheless better marks than the negative.","e":[30,43]}],"gemuet":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:162","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-174.0","de":"Die Neigung ist eine Disposition des Gemüths etwas zu lieben, und davon eingenommen zu seyn.","d":[37,44],"en":"Inclination is a disposition of the mind to love something and to be taken with it.","e":[36,40]}],"seele":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:106","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-003.1","de":"Merckmahle der Verschiedenheit aber sind, daß jene mit einer vernünftigen Seele begabt sind, diese aber gar keine Vernunft haben.","d":[74,79],"en":"Marks of difference, however, are that the former are endowed with a rational soul, the latter have no reason at all.","e":[78,82]}],"geist":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:630","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-016.4","de":"Ferner ist es ja eben auch nichts unmögliches, daß Geister uns sinnlich erscheinen könnten, ob es gleich nicht ausgemacht ist.","d":[51,58],"en":"Further, it is indeed also nothing impossible that spirits could appear to us sensibly, even though it is not settled.","e":[51,58]}],"vermoegen":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 119","link":"meier:meier-para-119.3","de":"Das Vermögen zu denken ist ein unzureichendes Merkmal eines Geistes, dass er aber Verstand hat, ein zureichendes.","d":[4,12],"en":"The faculty of thinking is an insufficient mark of a spirit; but that it has understanding, a sufficient one.","e":[4,11]}],"erkenntnisvermoegen":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:610","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-006.12","de":"Alle unsere Erkenntniße haben zwo Qvellen die Sinne und den Verstand; beide zusammen machen das Erkenntnißvermögen aus.","d":[96,114],"en":"All our cognitions have two sources, the senses and the understanding; both together make up the cognitive faculty.","e":[97,114]}],"kraft":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:618","link":"busolt:busolt-s05-029.4","de":"Die Empfindungen sind gewiße Veränderungen unseres Zustandes, wodurch alle unsere Erkenntniß Kräfte belebt und angestrengt werden.","d":[93,99],"en":"Sensations are certain alterations of our state through which all our cognitive powers are enlivened and exerted.","e":[80,86]}],"faehigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:100","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-195.0","de":"Diese Fähigkeit ein Systema zu formiren ist so vorzüglich, weil sie so selten ist, und zu gleich einen so großen Nutzen hat.","d":[6,15],"en":"This capacity to form a Systema is so excellent because it is so rare and at the same time of such great utility.","e":[5,13]}],"fertigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:138","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-312.2","de":"Das Laster ist also eine Fertigkeit, Handlungen zu ediren, welche denen moralischen Gesetzen entgegen sind.","d":[25,35],"en":"Vice is thus an aptitude for performing actions that are contrary to the moral laws.","e":[16,24]}],"geschicklichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:67","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-008.0","de":"Die Logick ist mehr eine Lehre der Geschicklichkeit, die vor den Jüngling gehöret, die Lehre der Weisheit aber gehöret vor den Mann.","d":[35,51],"en":"Logic is more a doctrine of skill, which belongs to the youth; the doctrine of wisdom, however, belongs to the man.","e":[28,33]}],"begehrungsvermoegen":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:26","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-059.1","de":"Erkenntniß-Kraft und Begehrungsvermögen.","d":[21,39],"en":"The power of cognition and the faculty of desire.","e":[31,48]}],"begierde":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:187","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-330.1","de":"Denn ein Vorurtheil ist ja nichts anders als die blose Begierde urtheilen zu wollen, jedoch ohne den gehörigen Scharfsinn oder Überlegung.","d":[55,63],"en":"For a prejudice is nothing other than the mere desire to want to judge, yet without the proper acumen or reflection.","e":[47,53]}],"neigung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:641","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-023.3","de":"Beim Vorurtheil ist die Vernunft nur leidend, denn es entsteht aus der Neigung, diese ist an sich passiue.","d":[71,78],"en":"In prejudice reason is only passive, for it arises from inclination, this is in itself passive.","e":[56,67]}],"hang":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:642","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-027.0","de":"Uebereilung ist ein Mangel der Ueberlegung des Verstandes Vorurtheil geschieht durch einen Hang nicht durch Uebereilung.","d":[91,95],"en":"Precipitancy is a lack of the reflection of the understanding; prejudice happens through a propensity, not through precipitancy.","e":[91,101]}],"gefuehl":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:60","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-116.2","de":"Setzet dem Gefühl eine Vernünftige Erkenntniß voraus, so ist es eine Vernünftige Lust, und Gefühl.","d":[11,17],"en":"If the feeling presupposes a rational cognition, it is a rational pleasure and feeling.","e":[7,14]}],"lust":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:60","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-116.2","de":"Setzet dem Gefühl eine Vernünftige Erkenntniß voraus, so ist es eine Vernünftige Lust, und Gefühl.","d":[81,85],"en":"If the feeling presupposes a rational cognition, it is a rational pleasure and feeling.","e":[66,74]}],"vergnuegen":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 237","link":"meier:meier-para-237.0","de":"Das Vergnügen (voluptas) ist die anschauende Erkenntniss der Vollkommenheit, und die anschauende Erkenntniss der Unvollkommenheit ist das Missvergnügen (taedium).","d":[4,13],"en":"Pleasure (voluptas) is the intuitive cognition of perfection, and the intuitive cognition of imperfection is displeasure (taedium).","e":[0,8]}],"wille":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:640","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-013.0","de":"Sie scheinen sich auf den Willen zu beziehen, und beziehen sich auch wirklich auf ihn: Das annehmen gilt nur da, wo keine apodictische Gewißheit ist.","d":[26,32],"en":"They seem to relate to the will, and also actually relate to it: Accepting holds only where there is no apodictic certainty.","e":[27,31]}],"willkuer":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:254","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-012.2","de":"Wenn der Mensch alles der Willkühr unterwerfen kann, so ist er das vollkommenste unter allen Wesen, und daher werden ihm die Willkührlichen Erdichtungen auch ofters sehr nützlich seyn.","d":[26,34],"en":"If the human being can subject everything to his power of choice, then he is the most perfect among all beings, and therefore arbitrary fictions will often be very useful to him too.","e":[49,64]}],"freiheit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:666","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-004.5","de":"Der Form nach sind Praktische Sazze solche nach denen eine Ausübung moglich ist, hiebei ist nicht das Verhältniß der Erkentniße sondern das Verhältniß der Freyheit.","d":[155,163],"en":"According to form, practical propositions are those according to which an exercise is possible; here it is not the relation of cognitions but the relation of freedom.","e":[158,165]}],"urteil":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:161","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-169.0","de":"Dieses Urtheil ist also mit nichten Dogmatisch, sonderen es ist blos noch allemahl mit einem gewißen Aufschub verbunden.","d":[7,14],"en":"This judgment is therefore by no means dogmatic, but is still always merely connected with a certain postponement.","e":[5,13]}],"satz":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:678","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-028.0","de":"Von der Folge auf den Grund, denn der Saz ist alsdenn nicht affirmation, weil eine Folge mehr als einen Grund haben kann.","d":[38,41],"en":"From the consequence to the ground, for the proposition is then not an affirmation, because a consequence can have more than one ground.","e":[44,55]}],"grundsatz":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:641","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-023.0","de":"Man pflegt auch das ein Vorurtheil zu nennen, was aus dem Vorurtheil fließt, und so ist ein wirkliches Vorurtheil ein Grundsaz.","d":[118,126],"en":"One is also wont to call that a prejudice which flows from prejudice, and thus an actual prejudice is a principle.","e":[104,113]}],"prinzip":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:683","link":"busolt:busolt-s31-008.2","de":"Bey der Synthetischen geht man von Prinzipien zu Principata, bey der andern umgekehrt, so ist die ganze Mathematik Synthetisch.","d":[35,45],"en":"In the synthetic one goes from principles to principata, in the other conversely; thus the whole of mathematics is synthetic.","e":[31,41]}],"lehrsatz":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 325","link":"meier:meier-para-325.1","de":"Jene heissen Lehrsätze (theorema), diese aber Aufgaben (problema).","d":[13,22],"en":"The former are called theorems (theorema), the latter however problems (problema).","e":[22,30]}],"axiom":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:668","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-012.2","de":"Axiom bedeutet soviel als eine Würde die an sich selbst deutlich ist, und nicht darf erwiesen werden, sie bringt schon eine Gewißheit mit sich.","d":[0,5],"en":"Axiom means as much as a dignity that is distinct in itself, and need not be proved; it already brings certainty with it.","e":[0,5]}],"aufgabe":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 337","link":"meier:meier-para-337.0","de":"Eine Aufgabe ist nicht genau, wenn sie zwar wahr und vollständig ist, aber durch Umwege führt, und zu viel in sich enthält §.334.","d":[5,12],"en":"A problem is not exact if it is indeed true and complete, but leads through detours, and contains too much in itself §.334.","e":[2,9]}],"praedikat":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 302","link":"meier:meier-para-302.2","de":"Ein allgemein verneinendes Urtheil ist wahr, wenn das Prädicat allen unter dem Subjecte enthaltenen zuwider ist §.301.","d":[54,62],"en":"A universal negative judgment is true if the predicate is repugnant to all those contained under the subject §.301.","e":[45,54]}],"kopula":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:664","link":"busolt:busolt-s25-004.0","de":"c.) Die Copula ist das, wodurch das Verhältniß der conceptuum bezeichnet wird.","d":[8,14],"en":"c.) The copula is that by which the relation of the conceptuum is designated.","e":[8,14]}],"verbindungsbegriff":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 293","link":"meier:meier-para-293.1","de":"Die Vorstellung der Übereinstimmung mehrerer Begriffe ist der Verbindungsbegriff (copula).","d":[62,80],"en":"The representation of the agreement of several concepts is the concept of connection (copula).","e":[63,84]}],"verneinung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 294","link":"meier:meier-para-294.7","de":"Die Beschaffenheit der Urtheile (qualitas iudicii) besteht in ihrer Bejahung und Verneinung.","d":[81,91],"en":"The quality of judgments (qualitas iudicii) consists in their affirmation and negation.","e":[78,86]}],"bejahung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 294","link":"meier:meier-para-294.7","de":"Die Beschaffenheit der Urtheile (qualitas iudicii) besteht in ihrer Bejahung und Verneinung.","d":[68,76],"en":"The quality of judgments (qualitas iudicii) consists in their affirmation and negation.","e":[62,73]}],"bejahend":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:673","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-002.0","de":"Ein Vernunftschluß ist bejahend, wenn die Conclusion bejahend ist, und verneinend, wenn die Conclusion verneinend ist.","d":[23,31],"en":"An inference of reason is affirmative when the conclusion is affirmative, and negative when the conclusion is negative.","e":[26,37]}],"verneinend":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:673","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-002.0","de":"Ein Vernunftschluß ist bejahend, wenn die Conclusion bejahend ist, und verneinend, wenn die Conclusion verneinend ist.","d":[71,81],"en":"An inference of reason is affirmative when the conclusion is affirmative, and negative when the conclusion is negative.","e":[78,86]}],"unendlich":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 383","link":"meier:meier-para-383.2","de":"Ist der mittlere Hauptbegriff verneinend, so ist der Untersatz unendlich §.376, und also doch ein bejahendes Urtheil §.294.","d":[63,72],"en":"If the middle principal concept is negative, the minor premise is infinite §.376, and so nevertheless an affirmative judgment §.294.","e":[66,74]}],"allgemein":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-001.8","de":"Das allgemeine Kriterium der Wahrheit ist hier also bloß Formale, die Uebereinstimmung des Erkenntnißes mit dem obiect.","d":[4,14],"en":"The universal criterion of truth is here, then, merely formal, the agreement of cognition with the object.","e":[4,13]}],"besonder":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:658","link":"busolt:busolt-s21-002.9","de":"Der Praecision ist entgegen die Tautologie, da dasselbe Merkmahl zweimahl, wiewohl besondere mahl versteckt vorkömmt.","d":[83,92],"en":"Opposed to precision is tautology, where the same mark occurs twice, though on particular occasions concealed.","e":[79,89]}],"einzeln":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:99","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-183.0","de":"Das Object der Dogmatum sind keine einzelne Dinge, sonderen allgemeine Eigenschaften, und Beschaffenheiten der Dinge.","d":[35,43],"en":"The object of Dogmata is not individual things, but universal properties and constitutions of things.","e":[29,39]}],"kategorisch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-006.6","de":"Dies Urtheil ist der Qualitaet nach bejahend, der Quantitaet nach allgemein, der Relation nach Kategorisch, der Modalitaet nach Aßertorisch.","d":[95,106],"en":"This judgment is, according to quality, affirmative, according to quantity, universal, according to relation, categorical, according to modality, assertoric.","e":[110,121]}],"hypothetisch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:672","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-055.4","de":"Bey den Hypothetischen ist nur bloß das Verhältniß zweierley Urtheile, wie eins aus der Richtigkeit des andern folgt.","d":[8,22],"en":"In hypothetical ones there is merely the relation of two judgments, how one follows from the correctness of the other.","e":[3,15]}],"disjunktiv":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:277","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-011.6","de":"Ein disjunctives Urtheil ist nichts mehr als eine Vorstellung einer logischen Eintheilung, oder Repraesentatio Divisionis Logicae.","d":[4,16],"en":"A disjunctive judgment is nothing more than a representation of a logical division, or Repraesentatio Divisionis Logicae.","e":[2,13]}],"problematisch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-012.4","de":"Bei den Problematischen Urtheilen bleibt also die Folge klar, der Grund aber, oder der eine Vordersaz ist unausgemacht.","d":[8,23],"en":"In problematic judgments, therefore, the consequence remains clear, but the ground, or the one antecedent, is undecided.","e":[3,14]}],"assertorisch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-006.6","de":"Dies Urtheil ist der Qualitaet nach bejahend, der Quantitaet nach allgemein, der Relation nach Kategorisch, der Modalitaet nach Aßertorisch.","d":[128,139],"en":"This judgment is, according to quality, affirmative, according to quantity, universal, according to relation, categorical, according to modality, assertoric.","e":[146,156]}],"apodiktisch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:225","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-576.0","de":"Von der apodictischen Gewisheit ist noch verschieden die mathematische gewisheit in der Anschauung, die evident ist.","d":[8,21],"en":"Different still from apodictic certainty is mathematical certainty in intuition, which is evident.","e":[21,30]}],"quantitaet":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:262","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-039.1","de":"Die Fictiones Aestheticae der Qualitaet nach sind die besten, die der Quantitaet nach aber sind nicht eben die besten.","d":[70,80],"en":"The Fictiones Aestheticae according to quality are the best, but those according to quantity are not exactly the best.","e":[84,92]}],"qualitaet":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:262","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-039.1","de":"Die Fictiones Aestheticae der Qualitaet nach sind die besten, die der Quantitaet nach aber sind nicht eben die besten.","d":[30,39],"en":"The Fictiones Aestheticae according to quality are the best, but those according to quantity are not exactly the best.","e":[39,46]}],"relation":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-077.0","de":"Relationes aber sind: mit einem Ding im Verhältniß auf andere. und in Beziehung anderer Dinge sich zutragende Veränderungen.","d":[0,10],"en":"Relationes, however, are: alterations that occur with a thing in relation to others, and in relation to other things.","e":[0,10]}],"modalitaet":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:665","link":"busolt:busolt-s25-012.9","de":"Anmerkung Diese Modalitaet ist höchst wichtig: denn wie oft wird nicht Möglichkeit und Nothwendigkeit mit einander verwechselt.","d":[16,26],"en":"Remark: This modality is of the highest importance: for how often are possibility and necessity not confused with one another.","e":[13,21]}],"verhaeltnis":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:672","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-055.4","de":"Bey den Hypothetischen ist nur bloß das Verhältniß zweierley Urtheile, wie eins aus der Richtigkeit des andern folgt.","d":[40,50],"en":"In hypothetical ones there is merely the relation of two judgments, how one follows from the correctness of the other.","e":[41,49]}],"analytisch":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 423","link":"meier:meier-para-423.0","de":"Die analytische Lehrart ist sehr unbequem, wenn man ein weitläuftiges Lehrgebäude nach ihr abhandeln, oder lernen wollte.","d":[4,15],"en":"The analytic method is very inconvenient if one wants to treat or learn an extensive system according to it.","e":[4,12]}],"synthetisch":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 422","link":"meier:meier-para-422.4","de":"Folglich ist die gelehrte Lehrart entweder synthetisch oder analytisch, sie mag nun demonstrativisch sein oder nicht §.421.","d":[43,54],"en":"Consequently the learned method is either synthetic or analytic, whether it be demonstrative or not §.421.","e":[42,51]}],"a-priori":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:206","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-465.3","de":"Apodictische urtheile sind Urtheile a priori, und dergleichen Erkenntnißen sind Dogmata, dergleichen ist z.E. die Mathematic.","d":[36,44],"en":"Apodictic judgments are judgments a priori, and such cognitions are dogmata; of this kind, e.g., is mathematics.","e":[34,42]}],"a-posteriori":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:653","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-007.3","de":"Sinnliche Erkentniße a posteriori heißen empirische. conceptus sensitiui sind, wo das obiect durch die Sinne gegeben wird.","d":[21,33],"en":"Sensible cognitions a posteriori are called empirical. Conceptus sensitivi are where the object is given through the senses.","e":[20,32]}],"empirisch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:653","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-007.3","de":"Sinnliche Erkentniße a posteriori heißen empirische. conceptus sensitiui sind, wo das obiect durch die Sinne gegeben wird.","d":[41,51],"en":"Sensible cognitions a posteriori are called empirical. Conceptus sensitivi are where the object is given through the senses.","e":[44,53]}],"rein":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:238","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-643.2","de":"Ein Beweis aus der Vernunft ist also nicht allemahl ein Beweis der reinen Vernunft ohne Anwendung der Erfahrung.","d":[67,73],"en":"A proof from reason is therefore not always a proof of pure reason without application of experience.","e":[55,59]}],"unrein":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 309","link":"meier:meier-para-309.2","de":"Jenes ist ein unreines (iudicium modale, modificatum, complexum qua copulam), dieses aber ein reines Urtheil (iudicium purum), z.E. diese Welt ist nothwendig da, sie ist nicht nothwendig da.","d":[14,22],"en":"The former is an impure judgment (iudicium modale, modificatum, complexum qua copulam), the latter however a pure judgment (iudicium purum), e.g. this world exists necessarily, it does not exist necessarily.","e":[17,23]}],"entgegensetzung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 287","link":"meier:meier-para-287.3","de":"Folglich sind der eingetheilte Begriff, und die Glieder der Eintheilung, wenn sie durch eine Entgegensetzung zusammen genommen werden, Wechselbegriffe §.262, und die Eintheilung muss den eingetheilten Begriff erschöpfen.","d":[93,108],"en":"Consequently the divided concept and the members of the division, when they are taken together by an opposition, are reciprocal concepts §.262, and the division must exhaust the divided concept.","e":[101,111]}],"kontradiktorisch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:64","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-135.0","de":"Die Unvollkommenheit, welche das contradictorische Gegentheil ist, heißet der Mangel und die Unvollkommenheit, die das Real Gegentheil vom Vollkommenen ist, heißt der Fehler.","d":[33,50],"en":"The imperfection that is the contradictory opposite is called the lack, and the imperfection that is the real opposite of the perfect is called the fault.","e":[29,42]}],"umkehrung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:671","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-044.8","de":"Bei der conversion der Urtheile heißt das Urtheil was umgekehrt werden soll: Judicium conversum das wodurch die Umkehrung entspringt iudicium convertens.","d":[112,121],"en":"In the conversion of judgments the judgment that is to be turned about is called: Judicium conversum; that through which the conversion arises, iudicium convertens.","e":[7,17]}],"kontraposition":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:282","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-028.3","de":"Die Regel der Contraposition ist diese: allgemein bejahende Urtheile laßen sich nur contraponiren.","d":[14,28],"en":"The rule of contraposition is this: universal affirmative judgments can only be contraposed.","e":[12,26]}],"widerspruch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:85","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-051.0","de":"Ein Wiederspruch ist freylich nichts anders als eine Begebenheit, da der eine sagt: ja, der andere aber hingegen: Nein.","d":[4,16],"en":"A contradiction is indeed nothing other than an occurrence in which the one says: yes, but the other, on the contrary: No.","e":[2,15]}],"satz-des-widerspruchs":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 363","link":"meier:meier-para-363.1","de":"Widrigenfalls müssten zwei widersprechende Urtheile zugleich wahr sein §.343, und das ist wider den Satz des Widerspruchs §.362.","d":[100,121],"en":"Otherwise two contradictory judgments would have to be true at the same time §.343, and that is contrary to the principle of contradiction §.362.","e":[112,138]}],"inhalt":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:667","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-005.2","de":"Die Logic aber, die von allem Inhalt abstrahirt, weiß davon nichts, daß einige Erkentniße so fruchtbar sind.","d":[30,36],"en":"But logic, which abstracts from all content, knows nothing of the fact that some cognitions are so fruitful.","e":[36,43]}],"umfang":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 262","link":"meier:meier-para-262.0","de":"Der Inbegriff aller Begriffe, die unter einem abgesonderten Begriffe enthalten sind, ist der Umfang desselben (sphaera notionis).","d":[93,99],"en":"The aggregate of all concepts that are contained under an abstracted concept is its extension (sphaera notionis).","e":[84,93]}],"sphaere":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:656","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-019.11","de":"Ein Conceptus muß eine Sphäre haben, conceptus der den andern in sich begreift heißt genus, der in andern enthalten ist, heißt species.","d":[23,29],"en":"A conceptus must have a sphere; the conceptus that comprehends the other in itself is called genus, that which is contained in others is called species.","e":[24,30]}],"gattung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:181","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-303.3","de":"Es ist dieses eine Gattung von einem inneren Betruge. man aestimiret nemlich das Alte und per consequentiam auch die Alten.","d":[19,26],"en":"This is a kind of inner deception. One namely aestimates the old and per consequentiam also the ancients.","e":[10,14]}],"art":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.9","de":"Was so vielen indiuiduen zukommt, die nur je gewesen, das kommt allen andern dieser Art zu d.i. was wir induction nennen.","d":[84,87],"en":"What belongs to so many individuals as have ever existed, that belongs to all others of this kind, i.e. what we call induction.","e":[93,97]}],"unterschied":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:674","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-009.3","de":"Es ist aber hierin kein anderer Unterschied, als daß die Schlüße in denen die Form versteckt ist außerordentliche sind.","d":[32,43],"en":"But there is in this no other difference than that the inferences in which the form is hidden are extraordinary.","e":[30,40]}],"definition":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-012.9","de":"Daß die Definizion des Urtheils nicht so evident ist, kommt daher weil wir schon urtheilen, wenn wir definiren.","d":[8,18],"en":"That the definition of the judgment is not so evident comes from the fact that we already judge when we define.","e":[9,19]}],"erklaerung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:81","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-006.2","de":"Dieses ist aber ja Identitas idem per idem, nichts, sagten die Scepticer, ist ein Circul in der Erklärung der Wahrheit.","d":[96,105],"en":"But this is indeed Identitas idem per idem, nothing, said the skeptics, is a circle in the definition of truth.","e":[91,101]}],"beschreibung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:77","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s05-008.1","de":"Wenn er aber in Ansehung dieses großen Nutzens fühllos ist, wird ihm alle Beschreibung nichts helfen.","d":[74,86],"en":"But if he is insensible with regard to this great utility, no description will help him.","e":[62,73]}],"einteilung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:277","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-011.6","de":"Ein disjunctives Urtheil ist nichts mehr als eine Vorstellung einer logischen Eintheilung, oder Repraesentatio Divisionis Logicae.","d":[78,89],"en":"A disjunctive judgment is nothing more than a representation of a logical division, or Repraesentatio Divisionis Logicae.","e":[74,82]}],"glied":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 286","link":"meier:meier-para-286.2","de":"Desgleichen die Glieder der Untereintheilung (membra subdividentia), und der Nebeneintheilungen (membra codividentia) sind.","d":[16,23],"en":"Likewise what the members of the subdivision (membra subdividentia), and of the codivisions (membra codividentia) are.","e":[18,25]}],"unterabteilung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:661","link":"busolt:busolt-s22-002.2","de":"Die Subdiuision ist die Diuision eines Membri dividentis Z.E. Alle Menschen sind Gelehrte oder Ungelehrte.","d":[4,15],"en":"The subdivision is the division of a membrum dividens, e.g. All human beings are learned or unlearned.","e":[4,15]}],"dichotomie":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:661","link":"busolt:busolt-s22-004.6","de":"Die leichteste Eintheilung ist die Dichotomie.","d":[35,45],"en":"The easiest division is dichotomy.","e":[24,33]}],"zergliederung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:134","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-268.0","de":"Alle Begriffe werden deutlich gemacht durch die Zergliederung, das ist per analysin, da sie zuvor dunckel, und verworren waren.","d":[48,61],"en":"All concepts are made distinct through analysis, that is per analysin, since they were previously obscure and confused.","e":[39,47]}],"analysis":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:635","link":"busolt:busolt-s12-006.13","de":"Analysis eines Begriffs ist der Successiue auf die partial Vorstellungen geführte Begriff.","d":[0,8],"en":"Analysis of a concept is the concept successively led to the partial representations.","e":[0,8]}],"synthesis":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:656","link":"busolt:busolt-s20-007.2","de":"Die Mathematik fängt jederzeit mit Definizionen an, denn sie hats bloß mit gemachten Begriffen zu thun. sie ist eine reine Synthesis der größe.","d":[123,132],"en":"Mathematics always begins with definitions, for it has to do merely with made concepts. It is a pure synthesis of quantity.","e":[101,110]}],"zusammensetzung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:292","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s13-025.1","de":"Die Lehrart nach der Zertheilung eines gantzen Lehrgebäudes ist keine Lehr Art, die Art der Zusammensetzung der Theile macht das Lehrgebäude aus.","d":[92,107],"en":"The method according to the dismemberment of a whole doctrinal system is no method; the way of the composition of the parts makes up the doctrinal system.","e":[99,110]}],"vergleichung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:106","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-001.1","de":"Jene sind Bestimmungen in der Sache selbst, wodurch dieselbe schon ohne Vergleichung mit anderen Dingen erkanndt werden kann.","d":[72,84],"en":"The former are determinations in the thing itself, through which it can already be cognized without comparison with other things.","e":[100,110]}],"uebereinstimmung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-001.8","de":"Das allgemeine Kriterium der Wahrheit ist hier also bloß Formale, die Uebereinstimmung des Erkenntnißes mit dem obiect.","d":[70,86],"en":"The universal criterion of truth is here, then, merely formal, the agreement of cognition with the object.","e":[67,76]}],"streit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:296","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s16-006.2","de":"Dieses sind gute Mittel, einen sich vom Halße zu halten, und den Streit zu endigen, aber nicht die Wahrheit zu finden.","d":[65,71],"en":"These are good means of keeping someone off one's neck and of ending the conflict, but not of finding the truth.","e":[73,81]}],"schluss":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:674","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-009.3","de":"Es ist aber hierin kein anderer Unterschied, als daß die Schlüße in denen die Form versteckt ist außerordentliche sind.","d":[57,64],"en":"But there is in this no other difference than that the inferences in which the form is hidden are extraordinary.","e":[55,65]}],"vernunftschluss":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:678","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-023.4","de":"Die Disiunctiuen Vernunftschlüße bestehen darinn, daß der maior in mehr theile getheilt wird, die einander opponirt sind.","d":[17,32],"en":"The disjunctive inferences of reason consist in this, that the major is divided into several parts which are opposed to one another.","e":[16,36]}],"verstandesschluss":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:670","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-035.0","de":"Wird ein Urtheil aus einem andern gefolgert, ohne ein zwischen Urtheil, so ist dies ein Verstandesschluß, per iudicium intermedium ein Vernunftschluß, z.B. Alle Menschen sind Sterblich, also ist auch Caius sterblich.","d":[88,104],"en":"If a judgment is inferred from another without an intermediate judgment, then this is an inference of the understanding; per iudicium intermedium an inference of reason, e.g. All human beings are mortal, therefore Caius too is mortal.","e":[89,119]}],"folgerung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:286","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s12-015.0","de":"Hier redet der Autor von unmittelbahren Folgerungen, es schickt sich aber gar nicht, denn es sind ja gar keine Vernunft Schlüße sonderen nur Verstandes Schlüße.","d":[40,51],"en":"Here the author speaks of immediate consequences, but this is not at all fitting, for they are not inferences of reason at all but only inferences of the understanding.","e":[36,48]}],"obersatz":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 369","link":"meier:meier-para-369.0","de":"Diejenige Gattung der ordentlichen Vernunftschlüsse, in denen der mittlere Hauptbegriff in dem Subjecte des Obersatzes und in dem Prädicate des Untersatzes steht, heisst die erste Figur (figura prima ratiociniorum).","d":[108,118],"en":"That species of ordinary inferences of reason in which the middle principal concept stands in the subject of the major premise and in the predicate of the minor premise is called the first figure (figura prima ratiociniorum).","e":[113,126]}],"untersatz":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 383","link":"meier:meier-para-383.2","de":"Ist der mittlere Hauptbegriff verneinend, so ist der Untersatz unendlich §.376, und also doch ein bejahendes Urtheil §.294.","d":[53,62],"en":"If the middle principal concept is negative, the minor premise is infinite §.376, and so nevertheless an affirmative judgment §.294.","e":[49,62]}],"schlusssatz":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:289","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s12-025.0","de":"Der Circulus in demonstrando ist derjenige Fehler, wenn man den Schlußsatz in einem Beweise zu seinem eigenen Vordersatz annimmt.","d":[64,74],"en":"The Circulus in demonstrando is that mistake when one assumes the conclusion in a proof as its own antecedent.","e":[66,76]}],"vordersatz":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-012.4","de":"Bei den Problematischen Urtheilen bleibt also die Folge klar, der Grund aber, oder der eine Vordersaz ist unausgemacht.","d":[92,101],"en":"In problematic judgments, therefore, the consequence remains clear, but the ground, or the one antecedent, is undecided.","e":[95,105]}],"figur":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:676","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-014.1","de":"Es ist also Begattung eines ratiocinii mit einer consequentia immediata, diese findet bey den drey lezten Figuren statt.","d":[106,113],"en":"It is thus a mating of a ratiocinium with a consequentia immediata; this occurs in the last three figures.","e":[98,105]}],"induktion":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.15","de":"Durch die Induction machen wir allgemeine Säzze, und dieser Schluß ist a particulaire ad vniversale.","d":[10,19],"en":"Through induction we make universal propositions, and this inference is a particulaire ad vniversale.","e":[8,17]}],"analogie":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:287","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s12-018.1","de":"Die Analogie, und die Induction sind nur bloß die Krücken für unseren Verstand.","d":[4,12],"en":"Analogy and induction are merely the crutches for our understanding.","e":[0,7]}],"beweis":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:233","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-623.1","de":"Das ist ein ostensiver beweis, dabey man zeigt, daß das falsch sey was das gegentheil ist, also ein Apagogischer Beweiß.","d":[113,119],"en":"That is an ostensive proof, whereby one shows that what is the opposite is false, hence an apagogic proof.","e":[21,26]}],"beweisgrund":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:238","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-643.1","de":"Die beweise aus der Vernunft haben zwar zum Beweisgrunde solche Sätze, die aus der Vernunft entspringen, allein zum Theil entspringen diese Sätze ihrem ersten Ursprunge nach aus der Erfahrung.","d":[44,56],"en":"The proofs from reason have indeed as their ground of proof such propositions as arise from reason, but in part these propositions arise, according to their first origin, from experience.","e":[44,59]}],"demonstration":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:234","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-629.1","de":"Diese Probation ist aber nicht allgemein gültig, und wird daher unrecht von unserem Autore eine Demonstration genanndt.","d":[96,109],"en":"But this probation is not universally valid, and is therefore wrongly called a demonstration by our author.","e":[79,92]}],"betrugschluss":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 402","link":"meier:meier-para-402.0","de":"Ein Vernunftschluss, welcher in der Form unrichtig ist (paralogismus), wenn sein Fehler versteckt ist, wird ein Betrugschluss genennet (sophisma, fallacia, captio).","d":[112,125],"en":"An inference of reason which is incorrect in form (paralogismus), when its fault is hidden, is called a fallacy (sophisma, fallacia, captio).","e":[104,111]}],"paralogismus":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:288","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s12-020.0","de":"Ein jeder in der Form falscher Schluß ist ein Paralogismus. ein jeder falscher Schluß aber, der ein Mittel seyn soll, in dem anderen einen Irrthum hervorzubringen, heißt ein Sophisma. es giebt unterschiedene Sophismata, die mit vielen Nahmen könnten beleget werden, welches aber gar nicht nöthig ist. sonsten giebt es noch wohl einige Sophismata, die in der logica eine Stelle verdienen, denn einige von denenselben können wahrer, als die andere seyn. sonsten gedencket hier auch der Autor des Sophisma ignorationis elenchi. für uns aber ist nur dieses dabey zu bemercken: Derjenige, der beym Streit die Streitfrage vergißt, begehet ein Sophisma ignorationis elenchi.","d":[46,58],"en":"Every inference false in form is a paralogism. But every false inference that is supposed to be a means of producing an error in another is called a sophism. There are various sophisms that could be given many names, which however is not at all necessary. Otherwise there are still some sophisms that deserve a place in logic, for some of them can be truer than the others. Otherwise the author also mentions here the Sophisma ignorationis elenchi. But for us only this is to be noted about it: he who in a conflict forgets the question in dispute commits a Sophisma ignorationis elenchi.","e":[35,45]}],"sophisma":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.26","de":"Sophisma ist eine dialectische Schlußart, die blos den Schein der Wahrheit hat.","d":[0,8],"en":"A sophism is a dialectical kind of inference that has merely the semblance of truth.","e":[2,9]}],"zirkel":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:81","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-006.2","de":"Dieses ist aber ja Identitas idem per idem, nichts, sagten die Scepticer, ist ein Circul in der Erklärung der Wahrheit.","d":[82,88],"en":"But this is indeed Identitas idem per idem, nothing, said the skeptics, is a circle in the definition of truth.","e":[77,83]}],"unmittelbar":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:119","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-122.1","de":"Eine Vorstellung aber ist dunckel (um zu unserer Materie zurück zu kehren) der man sich unmittelbahr nichtbewust ist.","d":[88,100],"en":"But a representation is obscure (to return to our matter) of which one is not immediately conscious.","e":[78,89]}],"mittelbar":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:230","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-613.0","de":"Ein jedweder gewiser Satz ist entweder unerweislich, oder unmittelbahr, oder mittelbahr, oder Erweislich gewiß.","d":[77,87],"en":"Every certain proposition is either indemonstrable, or immediate, or mediate, or demonstrably certain.","e":[57,64]}],"logik":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:39","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s02-091.2","de":"Eine Logica aber , die so dun ckel und übermäßig verfeineret ist, als des Crusii seine, kann diesen Nutzen nicht haben.","d":[5,11],"en":"A logic, however, that is as obscure and excessively refined as that of Crusius cannot have this utility.","e":[2,7]}],"vernunftlehre":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:24","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-047.0","de":"Es giebt viele Erkenntniße, deren Form nicht rational ist, und als denn ist es keine Vernunft-Lehre.","d":[85,99],"en":"There are many cognitions whose form is not rational, and then it is no doctrine of reason.","e":[72,90]}],"organon":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:20","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-032.9","de":"Die Logic, die ein Organon der rationalen Gelahrtsamkeit ist, geht nicht auf Historische, sonderen rationalische Erkenntniße.","d":[19,26],"en":"The logic that is an organon of rational erudition does not concern historical but rational cognitions.","e":[21,28]}],"kanon":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:610","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-010.7","de":"Die Logic ist vielmehr ein Kanon d.i. sie enthält Regeln, die sich allein auf den Verstand gründen, und auch nur a priori können demonstriret werden.","d":[27,32],"en":"Logic is rather a canon, i.e. it contains rules that are grounded solely on the understanding, and also can be demonstrated only a priori.","e":[18,23]}],"methode":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:75","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-076.1","de":"Die Methoden deren man sich heut zu Tage bedienet, das Frauenzimmer zu unterweisen, sind Wege sie zu Pedanten zu machen.","d":[4,12],"en":"The methods that are used nowadays to instruct women are ways of making them into pedants.","e":[4,11]}],"lehrart":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 423","link":"meier:meier-para-423.0","de":"Die analytische Lehrart ist sehr unbequem, wenn man ein weitläuftiges Lehrgebäude nach ihr abhandeln, oder lernen wollte.","d":[16,23],"en":"The analytic method is very inconvenient if one wants to treat or learn an extensive system according to it.","e":[13,19]}],"vortrag":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:299","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s18-006.4","de":"Der mündliche Vortrag hat einen großen Vorzug vor dem schriftlichen, denn der mündliche ist nicht so künstlich, als der schriftliche.","d":[14,21],"en":"The oral lecture has a great advantage over the written, for the oral is not so artificial as the written.","e":[9,16]}],"schreibart":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 475","link":"meier:meier-para-475.1","de":"Der Wohlklang der Schreibeart (sonoritas stili) besteht in derjenigen Vollkommenheit, vermöge welcher sie den Ohren gefällt §.458.","d":[18,29],"en":"The euphony of the style of writing (sonoritas stili) consists in that perfection by virtue of which it pleases the ears §.458.","e":[19,24]}],"lehrgebaeude":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:280","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-018.10","de":"Scholia sind Sätze, die einem Lehrgebäude gar nicht als essentialia, sonderen nur als accidentalia hinzugesezet werden.","d":[30,41],"en":"Scholia are propositions that are added to a doctrinal system not at all as essentialia but only as accidentalia.","e":[45,61]}],"system":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:100","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-195.0","de":"Diese Fähigkeit ein Systema zu formiren ist so vorzüglich, weil sie so selten ist, und zu gleich einen so großen Nutzen hat.","d":[20,27],"en":"This capacity to form a Systema is so excellent because it is so rare and at the same time of such great utility.","e":[24,31]}],"kritik":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:182","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-306.2","de":"Die Alten sind bey uns das Original selbst, und daher die, welche über alles Urtheilen, und über alle Critic erhaben sind.","d":[102,108],"en":"The ancients are for us the original itself, and hence those who are sublimely raised above all judging and above all criticism.","e":[118,127]}],"wissenschaftlich":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:22","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-037.7","de":"Der Verstand, der in Abstracto urtheilen kan, heißt der feinere Wißenschaftliche Verstand.","d":[64,80],"en":"The understanding that can judge in abstracto is called the finer, scientific understanding.","e":[67,77]}],"historisch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:149","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-071.0","de":"Der Glaube dieser 2 Sätzen ist nicht historisch, sonderen Vernünftig, hergeleitet aus practischen Regeln der Vernunft.","d":[37,47],"en":"The faith in these 2 propositions is not historical but rational, derived from practical rules of reason.","e":[41,51]}],"historie":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 519","link":"meier:meier-para-519.1","de":"Jene ist die Geschichte der Natur und Kunst (historia naturae et artis), diese aber die Historie schlechtweg (historia stricte dicta).","d":[88,96],"en":"The former is the history of nature and art (historia naturae et artis), the latter, however, history simply (historia stricte dicta).","e":[18,25]}],"pedanterie":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:627","link":"busolt:busolt-s09-007.9","de":"Die Pedanterie ist also der Mangel der Popularitaet des Gelehrten Erkenntnißes.","d":[4,14],"en":"Pedantry is therefore the lack of popularity in learned cognition.","e":[0,8]}],"autor":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:234","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-629.1","de":"Diese Probation ist aber nicht allgemein gültig, und wird daher unrecht von unserem Autore eine Demonstration genanndt.","d":[84,90],"en":"But this probation is not universally valid, and is therefore wrongly called a demonstration by our author.","e":[100,106]}],"philosophie":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:68","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-015.2","de":"Es ist die wahre Philosophie der Faulen, wenn man von allen Dingen behauptet, sie seyen über unseren Horizont.","d":[17,28],"en":"It is the true philosophy of the lazy when one asserts of all things that they are above our horizon.","e":[15,25]}],"mathematik":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:206","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-465.3","de":"Apodictische urtheile sind Urtheile a priori, und dergleichen Erkenntnißen sind Dogmata, dergleichen ist z.E. die Mathematic.","d":[114,124],"en":"Apodictic judgments are judgments a priori, and such cognitions are dogmata; of this kind, e.g., is mathematics.","e":[100,111]}],"metaphysik":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:109","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-032.0","de":"Die Metaphysica ist diejenige Wißenschaft, vermittelst welcher wir den Terminum a priori der Subordinirten Merckmahlen aufsuchen.","d":[4,15],"en":"Metaphysics is that science by means of which we seek out the Terminum a priori of the subordinated marks.","e":[0,11]}],"theologie":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:243","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-662.8","de":"Der historische Glaube n wird allein in der Theologie erforderet, daß man etwas einer Aussage wegen vor wahr hält.","d":[44,53],"en":"Historical belief is required alone in theology, that one hold something true on account of a statement.","e":[39,47]}],"moral":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:633","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-022.29","de":"In der Moral muß man urtheilen, da ist aber kein Irrthum Unvermeidlich: denn sie hat eine gewiße euidenz bei sich.","d":[7,12],"en":"In morals one must judge, but there no error is unavoidable: for it has a certain evidentia with it.","e":[3,9]}],"aesthetik":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-343.1","de":"Die Praecision ist also blos eine Regel der Sparsamkeit, und der Klugheit, aber gantz und gar nicht des Geschmacks, und der Aesthetic.","d":[124,133],"en":"Precision is thus merely a rule of thrift and of prudence, but not at all of taste and of aesthetics.","e":[90,100]}],"ding":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:150","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-079.1","de":"So sind z.E. die Mathematische Sätze evident. wir sind aber vieler Dinge gewiß, ohne eine Evidenz dennoch davon zu haben.","d":[67,72],"en":"Thus, e.g., mathematical propositions are evident. But we are certain of many things without nevertheless having evidence of them.","e":[78,84]}],"sache":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-080.0","de":"Wenn die Merckmahle nicht weniger enthalten, als zur unterscheidung der Sache nöthig ist, so ist dieses eine Praecision.","d":[72,77],"en":"If the marks contain no less than is necessary for the distinction of the thing, then this is a precision.","e":[74,79]}],"wesen":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:116","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-101.0","de":"Dieses alles sind die Essentialia des worts Materie, und machen folglich zusammengenommen das Logische Wesen derselben aus.","d":[103,108],"en":"All this are the Essentialia of the word matter, and consequently, taken together, constitute its logical essence.","e":[106,113]}],"dasein":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:231","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-620.1","de":"Die Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes, von seinen Eigenschaften, von seinen würckungen sind nicht unerweislich, sonderen erweislich.","d":[16,22],"en":"The proofs of the existence of God, of his properties, of his effects are not unprovable, but provable.","e":[18,27]}],"existenz":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:66","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-001.3","de":"So waren z.E. die Alten in einer gäntzlichen Unwißenheit von der Existence der neuen Welt, sie hatten keine Historische Erkenntniß davon.","d":[65,74],"en":"So, e.g., the ancients were in complete ignorance of the existence of the new world; they had no historical cognition of it.","e":[57,66]}],"wirklichkeit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.14","de":"Diese Ausnamen nennt man im disputiren Instanzen die Regel hat als denn nur eine Wirklichkeit, in der Erfahrung zu schließen und da kann eine Ausname seyn, wenn nur nicht die ganze Größe aufgehoben wird.","d":[81,93],"en":"These exceptions are called instances in disputing; the rule then has only an actuality in inferring in experience, and there an exception can be, provided only that the whole magnitude is not cancelled.","e":[78,87]}],"moeglichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:115","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-091.0","de":"Die Modi sind also nicht rationata Essentiae in Ansehung ihrer Wahrheit, sonderen nur in Ansehung ihrer Möglichkeit.","d":[104,115],"en":"The Modi are therefore not rationata Essentiae with regard to their truth, but only with regard to their possibility.","e":[105,116]}],"unmoeglichkeit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 141","link":"meier:meier-para-141.2","de":"Diese Schlüsse gelten auch, wenn von der blossen Möglichkeit oder Unmöglichkeit die Rede ist.","d":[66,79],"en":"These inferences hold also when the talk is of mere possibility or impossibility.","e":[67,80]}],"notwendigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:229","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-602.3","de":"Diese Subjective Nothwendigkeit etwas anzunehmen, ist sehr täuschend, und wandelbahr, weil sie sich nicht im Objecto gründet.","d":[17,31],"en":"This subjective necessity of accepting something is very deceptive and changeable, because it is not grounded in the object.","e":[16,25]}],"zufaelligkeit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 93","link":"meier:meier-para-93.2","de":"Z.E. wer die Würklichkeit Gottes aus der Zufälligkeit dieser Welt überzeugend darthut, hat eine wahre gelehrte Erkenntniss.","d":[41,53],"en":"E.g. whoever demonstrates convincingly the actuality of God from the contingency of this world has a true learned cognition.","e":[69,80]}],"notwendig":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:113","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-062.0","de":"Nothwendige Merckmahle sind solche ad Essentiam pertinentia, ohne welche die Sache gantz und gar nicht gedacht werden kann.","d":[0,11],"en":"Necessary marks are such ad Essentiam pertinentia, without which the thing cannot be thought at all.","e":[0,9]}],"zufaellig":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 114","link":"meier:meier-para-114.3","de":"Weil der Irrthum bei jenen leichter zu vermeiden ist, so ist er grösser als der Irrthum in den zufälligen Wahrheiten §.112.","d":[95,105],"en":"Since error is easier to avoid in the former, it is greater than error in contingent truths §.112.","e":[74,84]}],"grund":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-012.4","de":"Bei den Problematischen Urtheilen bleibt also die Folge klar, der Grund aber, oder der eine Vordersaz ist unausgemacht.","d":[66,71],"en":"In problematic judgments, therefore, the consequence remains clear, but the ground, or the one antecedent, is undecided.","e":[76,82]}],"folge":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:662","link":"busolt:busolt-s24-012.4","de":"Bei den Problematischen Urtheilen bleibt also die Folge klar, der Grund aber, oder der eine Vordersaz ist unausgemacht.","d":[50,55],"en":"In problematic judgments, therefore, the consequence remains clear, but the ground, or the one antecedent, is undecided.","e":[41,52]}],"zureichend":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:638","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-008.1","de":"Meinen ist weder ein Subiectiuer noch obiectiuer, Glauben nur ein Subiectiuer Zureichender Grund des führwahrhaltens.","d":[78,90],"en":"Opining is neither a subjective nor an objective, believing only a subjective sufficient ground of holding-to-be-true.","e":[78,88]}],"bedingung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:674","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-003.2","de":"Ich muß sagen daß einem Dinge das zu komme, was die Bedingung der Regel ist, und dies muß doch bejahend seyn.","d":[52,61],"en":"I must say that to a thing belongs what is the condition of the rule, and this must surely be affirmative.","e":[47,56]}],"ursache":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:163","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-181.0","de":"Der so gefährliche Feind der Menschen, von dem wir schon oben geredet haben, ist eine der größten Ursachen zur überhitzung.","d":[98,106],"en":"The enemy of men that is so dangerous, of which we have already spoken above, is one of the greatest causes of overheating.","e":[101,107]}],"wirkung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:669","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-033.2","de":"Hier definire ich idem per idem, und ist eben so viel gesagt, als: Die Ursache dieser Wirkung ist verborgen.","d":[86,93],"en":"Here I define idem per idem, and it is said just as much as: The cause of this effect is hidden.","e":[79,85]}],"substanz":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:661","link":"busolt:busolt-s22-004.7","de":"Alle Substanzen sind entweder Körper; oder nicht; dies ist das Fundament aller Logischen Definizionen.","d":[5,15],"en":"All substances are either bodies or not; this is the foundation of all logical definitions.","e":[4,14]}],"beschaffenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:81","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-005.1","de":"Ist hingegen eine Erkenntniß der Beschaffenheit derjenigen Sache, die wir uns vorstellen gemäs, so ist dieselbe wahr.","d":[33,47],"en":"If, on the other hand, a cognition conforms to the constitution of the thing we represent to ourselves, it is true.","e":[51,63]}],"eigenschaft":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:99","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-183.0","de":"Das Object der Dogmatum sind keine einzelne Dinge, sonderen allgemeine Eigenschaften, und Beschaffenheiten der Dinge.","d":[71,84],"en":"The object of Dogmata is not individual things, but universal properties and constitutions of things.","e":[62,72]}],"bestimmung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:106","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-001.1","de":"Jene sind Bestimmungen in der Sache selbst, wodurch dieselbe schon ohne Vergleichung mit anderen Dingen erkanndt werden kann.","d":[10,22],"en":"The former are determinations in the thing itself, through which it can already be cognized without comparison with other things.","e":[15,29]}],"einheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:196","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-388.3","de":"Der zureichende Grund des Vorwahrhaltens, die Einheit, ist das jenige, wodurch eine Sache gesezet wird.","d":[46,53],"en":"The sufficient ground of holding-to-be-true, the unity, is that through which a thing is posited.","e":[49,54]}],"vielheit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 471","link":"meier:meier-para-471.0","de":"Um der Reinigkeit der gelehrten Schreibeart willen muss man vermeiden: 1) alle Zwitterwörter (vox hybrida), deren Theile aus verschiedenen Sprachen genommen sind; 2) alle grammatischen Fehler; 3) alle barbarischen Ausdrücke; 4) alle Ausdrücke aus fremden Sprachen, und fremde Wortfügungen, sie müssten denn schon das Bürgerrecht erhalten haben; 5) alle veralteten Ausdrücke und Wortfügungen; 6) alle neuen Wörter und Kunstwörter; 7) alle Vielheit der Ausdrücke, wenn man statt derselben sich Eines Ausdrucks bedienen kann, ob er gleich unrein ist §.469.","d":[438,446],"en":"For the sake of the purity of the learned style of writing one must avoid: 1) all hybrid words (vox hybrida), whose parts are taken from different languages; 2) all grammatical faults; 3) all barbarous expressions; 4) all expressions from foreign languages, and foreign constructions, unless they have already received the right of citizenship; 5) all obsolete expressions and constructions; 6) all new words and technical terms; 7) all multiplicity of expressions, if one can make use of One expression instead of them, although it is impure §.469.","e":null}],"mannigfaltige":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:656","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-019.4","de":"Der Umfang besteht in dem, was unter dem Begriff stehet, und was allem Mannigfaltigen zukommt.","d":[71,85],"en":"The extension consists in that which stands under the concept, and which belongs to all the manifold.","e":[92,100]}],"vernunftbegriff":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:127","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-192.2","de":"Unsere Vernunftbegriffe erhalten eine Sinnlichkeit wenn wir uns allgemeine Urtheile in Concreto vorstellen.","d":[7,23],"en":"Our concepts of reason acquire a sensibility when we represent universal judgments in Concreto.","e":null}],"transzendental":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:262","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-038.1","de":"Alle Begrife sind entweder empirische, oder transcendentale Vernunft-Begrife.","d":[44,59],"en":"All concepts are either empirical or transcendental concepts of reason.","e":[37,51]}],"raum":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:83","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-030.0","de":"Die Unwißenheit ist ein leerer Raum in unserem Kopf und verhindert noch deswegen keine wahre Kenntniß, wenn er sie nicht verbreitet.","d":[31,35],"en":"Ignorance is an empty space in our head and for that reason does not hinder any true acquaintance, if it does not spread it.","e":[22,27]}],"zeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:136","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-297.0","de":"Etwas ist uns im Anfang nicht begreiflich, was doch in der Folge der Zeit sehr leicht von uns begriffen werden kann.","d":[69,73],"en":"Something is not comprehensible to us at the beginning which in the course of time can nevertheless be comprehended by us very easily.","e":[78,82]}],"welt":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:192","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-364.1","de":"Sehr viele Gelahrte, und Schöndenckende Geister sind der Gelahrten Welt überhaupt wircklich oftmals mehr schadlich, als nützlich.","d":[67,71],"en":"Very many learned men and spirits who think beautifully are in general actually often more harmful than useful to the learned world.","e":[126,131]}],"natur":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:212","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-497.0","de":"Die menschliche Natur ist wircklich weit geneigter zu entscheiden, als immer zu prüfen und aus zu machen, als immer zu forschen.","d":[16,21],"en":"Human nature is actually far more inclined to decide than always to test and to establish, than always to inquire.","e":[6,12]}],"materie":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:52","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-070.0","de":"Die Erlernung, die der Form nach Historisch, der Materie nach aber vernünftig ist, heißt eine Historische Erkenntniß.","d":[49,56],"en":"The learning that is historical in form but rational in matter is called a historical cognition.","e":[56,62]}],"form":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:674","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-009.3","de":"Es ist aber hierin kein anderer Unterschied, als daß die Schlüße in denen die Form versteckt ist außerordentliche sind.","d":[78,82],"en":"But there is in this no other difference than that the inferences in which the form is hidden are extraordinary.","e":[79,83]}],"koerper":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:99","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-181.0","de":"Die Schwere der Cörper aber gehöret schon zur Erfahrung und ist eine Historische Erkenntniß a posteriori.","d":[16,22],"en":"The heaviness of bodies, however, already belongs to experience and is a historical cognition a posteriori.","e":[17,23]}],"bewegung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:622","link":"busolt:busolt-s06-018.0","de":"Eine praktische Vollkommenheit der Logic ist nicht möglich, denn sie wäre die Bewegung des Wollens, dies wird in der Moral vorgetragen.","d":[78,86],"en":"A practical perfection of logic is not possible, for it would be the motion of willing; this is set forth in moral philosophy.","e":[69,75]}],"veraenderung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-077.0","de":"Relationes aber sind: mit einem Ding im Verhältniß auf andere. und in Beziehung anderer Dinge sich zutragende Veränderungen.","d":[110,123],"en":"Relationes, however, are: alterations that occur with a thing in relation to others, and in relation to other things.","e":[26,37]}],"zustand":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:156","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-134.0","de":"Wenn wir aber endlich bey einer jeden Erkenntniß weder etwas affirmiren, noch negiren, so ist dieses der Zustand des Zero.","d":[105,112],"en":"But if finally, in any cognition, we neither affirm nor negate anything, this is the state of Zero.","e":[85,90]}],"teil":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:240","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-656.10","de":"Derjenige Conceptus, deßen Sphaera nur ein Theil von der Sphaera eines anderen Conceptus ist, heißt ein Conceptus angustior.","d":[43,48],"en":"That Conceptus whose Sphaera is only a part of the Sphaera of another Conceptus is called a Conceptus angustior.","e":[39,43]}],"ganzes":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:49","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-053.0","de":"Es ist kein Mensch, der nicht Metaphysische Urtheile hätte. eine Wißenschaft überhaupt wird bestehen aus den Erkenntnißen, die ein Gantzes ausmachen.","d":[131,138],"en":"There is no human being who has no metaphysical judgments. A science in general will consist of the cognitions that make up a whole.","e":[126,131]}],"einfach":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:83","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-023.0","de":"Es giebt Methoden allen Irrthum zu vermeiden, diese aber sind so einfach, daß man sie eben daher nicht achtet.","d":[65,72],"en":"There are methods of avoiding all error, but these are so simple that for that very reason one does not heed them.","e":[58,64]}],"ewigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:197","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-397.0","de":"Alle scheinbahre Urtheile hingegen veränderen sich täglich, je nachdem man mehr, oder weniger Gründe vor, und wieder die Sache erkennt. was aber wahrscheinlich ist, ist in alle Ewigkeit, so zu sagen, wahrscheinlich.","d":[177,185],"en":"All plausible judgments, on the other hand, change daily, according as one cognizes more or fewer grounds for and against the matter. But what is probable is, so to speak, probable to all eternity.","e":[188,196]}],"ordnung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 427","link":"meier:meier-para-427.0","de":"Die Kunst (ars) ist ein Inbegriff der Regeln, welche nach einer Ordnung gedacht werden.","d":[64,71],"en":"Art (ars) is a sum of rules that are thought according to an order.","e":[61,66]}],"zweck":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:630","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-016.12","de":"Eine genaue Erkenntniß ist eine solche, die mit dem Gegenstand in allen Stücken uebereinstimmt, und dem Zweck gemäß ist.","d":[104,109],"en":"An exact cognition is one that agrees with the object in all respects and is in accordance with the end.","e":[100,103]}],"mittel":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:296","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s16-006.2","de":"Dieses sind gute Mittel, einen sich vom Halße zu halten, und den Streit zu endigen, aber nicht die Wahrheit zu finden.","d":[17,23],"en":"These are good means of keeping someone off one's neck and of ending the conflict, but not of finding the truth.","e":[15,20]}],"gott":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:231","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-620.1","de":"Die Beweise vom Daseyn Gottes, von seinen Eigenschaften, von seinen würckungen sind nicht unerweislich, sonderen erweislich.","d":[23,29],"en":"The proofs of the existence of God, of his properties, of his effects are not unprovable, but provable.","e":[31,34]}],"schoepfung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:181","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-300.1","de":"Deme ohngeachtet aber findet man dennoch, daß gar keine Veränderung in denen Arten, und generibus der Geschöpfe vorgegangen sey, sonderen alles noch so beschaffen sey, wie bey Schöpfung der Welt und aller Dinge es gewesen.","d":[176,185],"en":"Notwithstanding this, one nevertheless finds that no alteration at all has taken place in the species and generibus of creatures, but that everything is still constituted as it was at the creation of the world and of all things.","e":[188,196]}],"vorsehung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 393","link":"meier:meier-para-393.2","de":"Zum Exempel: wenn eine Vorsehung GOttes ist, so sind alle ängstliche Sorgen vergeblich: nun ist das erste wahr, also auch das letzte; Oder 2) von der Unrichtigkeit des letztern auf die Unrichtigkeit des erstern §.364.","d":[23,32],"en":"For example: if there is a providence of GOD, all anxious cares are in vain: now the first is true, therefore also the last; Or 2) from the incorrectness of the latter to the incorrectness of the former §.364.","e":[27,37]}],"unsterblichkeit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 405","link":"meier:meier-para-405.1","de":"Zum Exempel: wenn man die Unsterblichkeit der Seele beweisen soll, und man beweiset ihre Unverweslichkeit.","d":[26,41],"en":"For example: if one is to prove the immortality of the soul, and one proves its incorruptibility.","e":[36,47]}],"qualitas-occulta":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:82","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-012.0","de":"Das eine will eben so viel sagen, als das andere, es ist dieses also eine Qualitas occulta.","d":[74,90],"en":"The one means just as much as the other; this is therefore a qualitas occulta.","e":[61,77]}],"pflicht":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:278","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-012.1","de":"Die logic nun hat die Pflicht, sie muß die exponible urtheile exprimiren. was bedeuten die Fragen: Quae?","d":[22,29],"en":"Logic now has the duty, it must express the exponible judgments. What do the questions mean: Quae?","e":[18,22]}],"gesetz":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:628","link":"busolt:busolt-s11-002.10","de":"Wesentlich sind sie wenn sie im Erkenntniß selbst beruhen und mit den obersten Gesezzen des Verstandes zusammenstimmen.","d":[79,87],"en":"They are essential if they rest in the cognition itself and agree with the highest laws of the understanding.","e":[83,87]}],"sittlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:149","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-070.0","de":"Diese 2 Sätze sind der einzige Grund aller Religion, Sittlichkeit etc. Diese 2 Sätze sind die wahre conditio sine qua non.","d":[53,65],"en":"These 2 propositions are the sole ground of all religion, morality etc. These 2 propositions are the true conditio sine qua non.","e":[58,66]}],"moralitaet":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:95","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-141.0","de":"Wenn gleich eine Speculation wircklich irrig ist, deswegen aber doch dieser Irrthum keinen Einfluß auf die Praxin, d.i. auf die Moralität der Sitten hat, so ist dieselbe in Ansehung der Sitten indifferent, und nicht so verabscheuenswürdig, als wenn sie auch die Sitten verdürbe.","d":[128,137],"en":"Even if a speculation is really erroneous, yet this error has no influence on Praxin, i.e. on the morality of conduct, then it is indifferent with regard to conduct, and not as detestable as if it also corrupted conduct.","e":[98,106]}],"tugend":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:654","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-012.3","de":"Z.E. Alle Begriffe von Farben, vom Geschmack sind conceptus dati a posteriori von der Tugend a priori.","d":[86,92],"en":"E.g. All concepts of colors, of taste are conceptus dati a posteriori; of virtue, a priori.","e":[74,80]}],"laster":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:684","link":"busolt:busolt-s31-010.6","de":"Eben diese auf andere Wißenschaften angewandt, ist blos vergeblich sonst verfällt man in das Laster der Methodenmanier.","d":[93,99],"en":"This same method, applied to other sciences, is merely in vain; otherwise one falls into the vice of method-mannerism.","e":[93,97]}],"glueckseligkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:111","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-045.1","de":"Nachdem nun die Folgen von werth sind, in Absicht auf die Vernunft oder auf unsere Vollkommenheit, und Glückseligkeit, so werden auch die Merckmahle als Erkenntniß-Gründe von werth seyn.","d":[103,117],"en":"Now according as the consequences are of worth with respect to reason or to our perfection and happiness, so too the marks as grounds of cognition will be of worth.","e":[95,104]}],"klugheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-343.1","de":"Die Praecision ist also blos eine Regel der Sparsamkeit, und der Klugheit, aber gantz und gar nicht des Geschmacks, und der Aesthetic.","d":[65,73],"en":"Precision is thus merely a rule of thrift and of prudence, but not at all of taste and of aesthetics.","e":[49,57]}],"weisheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:67","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-008.0","de":"Die Logick ist mehr eine Lehre der Geschicklichkeit, die vor den Jüngling gehöret, die Lehre der Weisheit aber gehöret vor den Mann.","d":[97,105],"en":"Logic is more a doctrine of skill, which belongs to the youth; the doctrine of wisdom, however, belongs to the man.","e":[79,85]}],"maxime":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:646","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-051.0","de":"a.) Die Maximen des dogmatischen Gebrauchs d.i. der Vorsaz sich seiner Vernunft so zu bedienen, daß man hoft zur apodictischen Gewißheit zu gelangen.","d":[8,15],"en":"a.) The maxims of the dogmatic use, i.e. the resolve to make use of one's reason in such a way that one hopes to attain apodictic certainty.","e":[8,14]}],"achtung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:176","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-275.1","de":"Dieses Vorurtheil entspringt nicht allein aus dem Bewust seyn unserer eigenen Schwäche, denn diese ist kein Grund anderen mehr zu zueignen, als uns selbst, sonderen aus einer gewißen Achtung, die wir vor das gantze Menschliche Geschlecht haben, da wir urtheilen, daß das, was uns fehle, doch bey anderen anzutreffen seyn werde.","d":[183,190],"en":"This prejudice arises not only from the consciousness of our own weakness, for this is no ground for ascribing more to others than to ourselves, but from a certain respect that we have for the whole human race, in that we judge that what is lacking to us will nevertheless be found in others.","e":[164,171]}],"recht":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:93","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-122.1","de":"Das ist ja das allgemeine Recht eines jeden Menschen, und der einzige sichere Weeg, zur Wahrheit zu gelangen.","d":[26,31],"en":"That is the universal right of every man, and the only sure way to arrive at truth.","e":[22,27]}],"gerechtigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:35","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s02-054.0","de":"3 tio Chilon ward bey den Lacedämoniern durch seine Gerechtigkeit und Geduldigkeit sichtbahr und achtbahr. sein Wahlspruch war: lerne nicht zu viel, sonderen dich selbst erkennen.","d":[52,65],"en":"3 tio Chilon became visible and respected among the Lacedaemonians through his justice and patience. His motto was: learn not too much, but know yourself.","e":[79,86]}],"gut":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:244","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-663.9","de":"Ein solcher Tugendthafter ist mit einem Creditore zu vergleichen, er hofet das künftige Gute, gesezt daß er auch davon noch keine Spur hat.","d":[88,92],"en":"Such a virtuous person is to be compared to a creditor; he hopes for the future good, supposing that he has as yet not a trace of it.","e":[80,84]}],"boese":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:196","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-389.0","de":"Mehr als zu reichend kann kein Grund seyn, denn sonsten ist er gantz, und gar kein Grund, eben so, als wie nichts mehr, als wahr, mehr als falsch, mehr als gut, mehr als Böse seyn kann, denn sonsten ist es nichts.","d":[170,174],"en":"No ground can be more than sufficient, for otherwise it is entirely and altogether no ground, just as nothing can be more than true, more than false, more than good, more than evil, for otherwise it is nothing.","e":[176,180]}],"interesse":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:651","link":"busolt:busolt-s17-017.9","de":"Die nothwendige Voraussezzung einer Erkenntniß mit dem praktischen Interesse ist glauben.","d":[67,76],"en":"The necessary presupposition of a cognition with practical interest is believing.","e":[59,67]}],"wohlgefallen":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 283","link":"meier:meier-para-283.0","de":"Weil die zu erklärenden Sachen viele wesentliche Stücke und Eigenschaften haben können, so kann man nach Wohlgefallen diejenigen aussuchen, die eine Worterklärung ausmachen §.282; wenn man nur übrigens die Regeln der Erklärungen beobachtet.","d":[105,117],"en":"Because the things to be defined can have many essential parts and properties, one can select at pleasure those that make up a nominal definition §.282; if only one otherwise observes the rules of definitions.","e":null}],"handlung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:138","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-312.2","de":"Das Laster ist also eine Fertigkeit, Handlungen zu ediren, welche denen moralischen Gesetzen entgegen sind.","d":[37,47],"en":"Vice is thus an aptitude for performing actions that are contrary to the moral laws.","e":[40,47]}],"gebrauch":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 452","link":"meier:meier-para-452.1","de":"Der Gebrauch der leeren Ausdrücke in den gelehrten Reden ist die Wortkrämerei der Gelehrten, da man Worte für Sachen verkauft.","d":[4,12],"en":"The use of empty expressions in learned discourses is the word-mongering of scholars, in which one sells words for things.","e":[4,7]}],"regel":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:149","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-071.0","de":"Der Glaube dieser 2 Sätzen ist nicht historisch, sonderen Vernünftig, hergeleitet aus practischen Regeln der Vernunft.","d":[98,104],"en":"The faith in these 2 propositions is not historical but rational, derived from practical rules of reason.","e":[89,94]}],"geschmack":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:618","link":"busolt:busolt-s05-029.5","de":"Der Geschmack ist das Vermögen der Sinnlichen Beurtheilungskraft nach allgemeinen Gesezzen der Sinnlichkeit.","d":[4,13],"en":"Taste is the faculty of the sensible power of judging according to general laws of sensibility.","e":[0,5]}],"schoenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:109","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-034.0","de":"Der Tiefsinn ist der Schönheit in gewißer Art entgegen, die Erkenntniß wird trocken, je mehr in ihr abstrahirt wird.","d":[21,30],"en":"Profundity is in a certain way opposed to beauty; cognition becomes dry the more it is abstracted.","e":[42,48]}],"schoen":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:201","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-431.1","de":"Dieses Subjective Hinderniß des Verstandes ist eine schöne Arbeit vor einen Philosophen, der den Menschen Studiren will.","d":[52,58],"en":"This subjective hindrance of the understanding is a beautiful task for a philosopher who wants to study human beings.","e":[52,61]}],"aesthetisch":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-342.0","de":"Bey schönen d.i. aesthetischen Erkenntnißen aber dagegen ist die Praecision wiederum eine entbehrliche Vollkommenheit.","d":[17,30],"en":"In beautiful, i.e., aesthetic cognitions, on the other hand, precision is in turn a dispensable perfection.","e":[20,29]}],"erhaben":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:182","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-306.2","de":"Die Alten sind bey uns das Original selbst, und daher die, welche über alles Urtheilen, und über alle Critic erhaben sind.","d":[109,116],"en":"The ancients are for us the original itself, and hence those who are sublimely raised above all judging and above all criticism.","e":[69,78]}],"nachahmung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:163","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-178.0","de":"Der Nachahmungs-Geist ist unter allem, was dem Philosophischen Geist nur schaden und entgegen seyn kann, allemahl wircklich der ärgste.","d":[4,15],"en":"The spirit of imitation is, among everything that can only harm and run counter to the philosophical spirit, always really the worst.","e":[14,23]}],"muster":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:47","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-045.1","de":"Muster, Nachahmungswürdige Muster sind nothwendig um den Geschmack zu bilden, und beyzubehalten.","d":[0,6],"en":"Models, models worthy of imitation, are necessary in order to form and maintain taste.","e":[0,6]}],"in-ansehung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:115","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-091.0","de":"Die Modi sind also nicht rationata Essentiae in Ansehung ihrer Wahrheit, sonderen nur in Ansehung ihrer Möglichkeit.","d":[45,56],"en":"The Modi are therefore not rationata Essentiae with regard to their truth, but only with regard to their possibility.","e":[47,61]}],"in-absicht-auf":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 137","link":"meier:meier-para-137.0","de":"Eine Erkenntniss, welche in Absicht auf die Stärke der Klarheit betrachtet wird, ist entweder deutlich, oder verworren §.14.","d":[25,39],"en":"A cognition considered with regard to the intensity of clarity is either distinct or confused §.14.","e":[23,37]}],"achtung-geben":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 309","link":"meier:meier-para-309.3","de":"Bei der Wahrheit der unreinen Urtheile muss man sonderlich, auf die Bestimmung des Verbindungsbegriffs und der Verneinung desselben, Achtung geben.","d":[133,146],"en":"In the truth of impure judgments one must pay particular attention to the determination of the concept of connection and of the negation of it.","e":[57,66]}],"nach-und-nach":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:619","link":"busolt:busolt-s05-030.5","de":"Empfindungen ueberraschen, Erkenntniß kommt nach und nach; jene sind etwas vorübergehendes, diese etwas Beständiges.","d":[44,57],"en":"Sensations take one by surprise, cognition comes gradually; those are something transitory, this something lasting.","e":[49,58]}],"zum-exempel":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:269","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-067.3","de":"Z.E. wenn er den Umkreiß einer Kugel, oder eines Vieleckes Peripherie nennet, da er doch Perimeter solte genannt werden.","d":[0,3],"en":"E.g. when he calls the circumference of a sphere, or of a polygon, Periphery, whereas it should be called Perimeter.","e":[0,4]}],"das-ist":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:680","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-031.9","de":"Was so vielen indiuiduen zukommt, die nur je gewesen, das kommt allen andern dieser Art zu d.i. was wir induction nennen.","d":[91,94],"en":"What belongs to so many individuals as have ever existed, that belongs to all others of this kind, i.e. what we call induction.","e":[99,103]}],"dictum-de-omni":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:673","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-006.2","de":"Die Beiden angeführten Regeln sind eben dies, was den alten dictum de omni et nullo war.","d":[60,83],"en":"The two rules cited are just what the dictum de omni et nullo was for the ancients.","e":[38,61]}],"nota-notae":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:673","link":"busolt:busolt-s27-003.0","de":"a.) Nota notae est Nota rei ipsius, dies gilt von bejahenden Urtheilen.","d":[4,34],"en":"a.) Nota notae est Nota rei ipsius; this holds of affirmative judgments.","e":[4,34]}],"petitio-principii":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 411","link":"meier:meier-para-411.0","de":"Wenn ein Schlusssatz aus Vordersätzen hergeleitet wird, welche eben so ungewiss sind als er selbst, so werden die Beweisthümer erbettelt (petitio principii seu quaesiti.)","d":[138,155],"en":"If a conclusion is derived from premises which are just as uncertain as it itself, the proofs are begged (petitio principii seu quaesiti.)","e":[106,123]}],"terminus-medius":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:675","link":"busolt:busolt-s29-006.1","de":"Es muß also nicht mehr geschloßen werden, als was in den Praemissen begriffen ist in den Praemissis ist maior, minor und Terminus medius.","d":[121,136],"en":"Thus no more must be inferred than what is comprehended in the premises; in the praemissis there are maior, minor and Terminus medius.","e":[118,133]}],"gegenteil":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:145","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-026.0","de":"Der Zureichende Grund aber ist derjenige, deßen Gegentheil unmöglich als wahr gedacht, und vorgestellet werden kann.","d":[48,58],"en":"But the sufficient ground is that whose opposite cannot be thought and represented as true.","e":[40,48]}],"grenze":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:78","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s05-012.0","de":"Die Grentzen, die wir unserer Wißbegierde sezten, sind so nothwendig, daß wir ohne dieselbe kaum eine andere Wißenschaft recht erkennen.","d":[4,12],"en":"The boundaries that we set to our desire for knowledge are so necessary that without them we hardly cognize any other science properly.","e":[4,14]}],"schranke":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:613","link":"busolt:busolt-s03-001.6","de":"Wolfs Logik ist die beste die mehresten dieser Männer sezten der Logic nicht die gehörige Schranken.","d":[90,99],"en":"Wolff's logic is the best; most of these men did not set the proper limits to logic.","e":[68,74]}],"einschraenkung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:640","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-013.2","de":"Um etwas anzunehmen darf ich eben nicht gewiß seyn, und dann habe ichs mit einer Einschränkung angenommen.","d":[81,94],"en":"In order to accept something I need not be certain, and then I have accepted it with a limitation.","e":[87,97]}],"verbindung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:256","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-021.6","de":"Mehrentheils ist bey den erdichteten Begrifen die Willkührliche Verbindung, und die Willkührliche Trennung mit einander combinirt.","d":[64,74],"en":"For the most part, in invented concepts arbitrary combination and arbitrary separation are combined with one another.","e":[50,61]}],"verknuepfung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:277","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s11-011.0","de":"Alles Verhaltniß in den Urtheilen ist entweder ein Verhältniß der Verknüpfung, oder ein Verhältniß des Wiederstreits.","d":[66,77],"en":"All relation in judgments is either a relation of connection or a relation of conflict.","e":[50,60]}],"zusammenhang":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:650","link":"busolt:busolt-s17-009.7","de":"Ein Beweis ist eine deutliche Erkentniß des richtigen Zusammenhangs eines Sazzes mit hinreichenden Gründen.","d":[54,67],"en":"A proof is a distinct cognition of the correct interconnection of a proposition with sufficient grounds.","e":[47,62]}],"beziehung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:114","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-077.0","de":"Relationes aber sind: mit einem Ding im Verhältniß auf andere. und in Beziehung anderer Dinge sich zutragende Veränderungen.","d":[70,79],"en":"Relationes, however, are: alterations that occur with a thing in relation to others, and in relation to other things.","e":[0,10]}],"absicht":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:627","link":"busolt:busolt-s10-003.1","de":"Die andern sind freilich Stolzer: denn sie sagen die freye Künste müßen nicht in der Absicht, als Handwerke gebraucht werden.","d":[85,92],"en":"The others are of course prouder: for they say that the free arts must not be used with that aim, as trades.","e":[93,96]}],"ursprung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:104","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-240.0","de":"Daß die Unwißenheit an sich nicht im geringsten ein Ursprung eines Irrthums seyn könne, ist im vorigen Paragrapho schon mit mehrerem angezeiget worden.","d":[52,60],"en":"That ignorance in itself cannot in the least be an origin of error has already been shown at greater length in the previous Paragraph.","e":[51,57]}],"quelle":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:298","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s17-007.1","de":"Die Geschichte ist compilirt, wenn ich sie nicht aus den ersten Quellen, sonderen von Spätern zusammengeschrieben.","d":[64,71],"en":"History is compiled if I have written it together not from the first sources but from later ones.","e":[69,76]}],"allgemeinheit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:621","link":"busolt:busolt-s06-011.1","de":"Die Mannigfaltigkeit, von dieser ist die Logische Allgemeinheit das Gegentheil.","d":[50,63],"en":"Manifoldness; the opposite of this is logical universality.","e":[46,58]}],"mannigfaltigkeit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:621","link":"busolt:busolt-s06-013.1","de":"Logische Vollkommenheit mit der aesthetischen verbunden nennt man Bündigkeit. aesthetic und Logic verbunden heißt: Mannigfaltigkeit.","d":[115,131],"en":"Logical perfection combined with the aesthetic one calls conciseness. Aesthetic and logic combined means: manifoldness.","e":[106,118]}],"grad":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:141","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-346.1","de":"Ein höherer Grad der Deutlichkeit der Erkenntniß hingegen durch Coordinirte Merckmahle ist die ausgebreitete Deutlichkeit.","d":[12,16],"en":"A higher degree of distinctness of cognition through coordinated marks, on the other hand, is extensive distinctness.","e":[9,15]}],"reihe":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:637","link":"busolt:busolt-s13-001.2","de":"Profunditas oder Gründlichkeit ist die Reihe der Subordinirten Merkmahle, oder den Merkmalen von den Merkmahlen.","d":[39,44],"en":"Profunditas or thoroughness is the series of the subordinated marks, or of the marks of the marks.","e":[35,41]}],"menge":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:258","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-027.1","de":"Die Sphaera notionis bedeutet eigentlich die Menge der Dinge, die unter einem Begrif, als eine Nota Communis begrifen sind.","d":[45,50],"en":"The Sphaera notionis properly signifies the multitude of things that are comprehended under a concept as a Nota Communis.","e":[44,53]}],"begebenheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:85","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-051.0","de":"Ein Wiederspruch ist freylich nichts anders als eine Begebenheit, da der eine sagt: ja, der andere aber hingegen: Nein.","d":[53,64],"en":"A contradiction is indeed nothing other than an occurrence in which the one says: yes, but the other, on the contrary: No.","e":[48,58]}],"dauer":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:74","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-065.0","de":"Viele Wißenschaften sind von der Art, daß mit der Dauer der Zeit durch ihren Umfang die Menschlichen Fähigkeiten noch überschritten werden.","d":[50,55],"en":"Many sciences are of such a kind that, with the duration of time, human capacities are still exceeded by their extension.","e":[48,56]}],"ausdehnung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:68","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s04-021.3","de":"Das nennt man Belesenheit, worinn sie einen Vorzug suchen. aber eben diese große Ausdehnung verursachet es, daß die Wißenschaft ihren Werth verlieret.","d":[81,91],"en":"This is called wide reading, in which they seek a distinction. But precisely this great extension causes the science to lose its value.","e":[88,97]}],"urbild":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:51","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-068.4","de":"Muster aber sind Beyspiele, die dem Urbild am meisten nahekommen.","d":[36,42],"en":"Models, however, are examples that come closest to the archetype.","e":[55,64]}],"naturgesetz":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 408","link":"meier:meier-para-408.5","de":"Z.E. die Jugend ist den Naturgesetzen gemäss, was den Naturgesetzen gemäss, das macht mich vollkommener, was mich vollkommener macht, dazu bin ich verbunden; also bin ich zur Tugend verbunden.","d":[24,37],"en":"E.g. youth accords with the laws of nature, what accords with the laws of nature, that makes me more perfect, what makes me more perfect, to that I am obligated; therefore I am obligated to virtue.","e":null}],"naturwissenschaft":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:657","link":"busolt:busolt-s20-011.4","de":"In der Naturwißenschaft finden descriptionen statt, und wenn ich mir mehreres in demselben Dinge denke; so erfordert dies eine declaration.","d":[7,23],"en":"In natural science descriptions take place, and if I think several things in the same thing, this requires a declaration.","e":[3,18]}],"weltweisheit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 5","link":"meier:meier-para-5.0","de":"Die Weltweisheit (philosophia) ist eine Wissenschaft der allgemeinern Beschaffenheiten der Dinge, in so ferne sie ohne Glauben erkannt werden.","d":[4,16],"en":"Philosophy (philosophia) is a science of the more general properties of things, insofar as they are cognized without faith.","e":[0,10]}],"grundbegriff":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:115","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-083.0","de":"Das Wesen einer Sache ist der erste zureichende Grundbegriff, welcher hinreichet um alles herzuleiten, was der ersteren zukommet.","d":[48,60],"en":"The essence of a thing is the first sufficient fundamental concept, which suffices to derive everything that belongs to the former.","e":[47,66]}],"hauptbegriff":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 383","link":"meier:meier-para-383.2","de":"Ist der mittlere Hauptbegriff verneinend, so ist der Untersatz unendlich §.376, und also doch ein bejahendes Urtheil §.294.","d":[17,29],"en":"If the middle principal concept is negative, the minor premise is infinite §.376, and so nevertheless an affirmative judgment §.294.","e":[14,31]}],"erfahrungsbegriff":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 255","link":"meier:meier-para-255.3","de":"Einen Erfahrungsbegriff erlangen wir entweder durch die unmittelbare, oder durch die mittelbare Erfahrung.","d":[6,23],"en":"We obtain a concept of experience either through immediate or through mediate experience.","e":[12,33]}],"vernunfterkenntnis":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:615","link":"busolt:busolt-s04-010.0","de":"Die Philosophie ist eine speculatiue VernunftErkenntniß nach Regeln in abstracto.","d":[37,55],"en":"Philosophy is a speculative rational cognition according to rules in abstracto.","e":[28,46]}],"erkenntnisgrund":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:265","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s10-046.2","de":"Zweitens müßen aber auch diese Merckmahle klare Erkenntnißgründe seyn.","d":[48,64],"en":"Secondly, however, these marks must also be clear grounds of cognition.","e":null}],"erkenntniskraft":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 61","link":"meier:meier-para-61.1","de":"Die Wahrheiten, die wir vergessen, sind ohnedem nicht ganz unnütz gewesen, weil sie den Grad unserer Erkenntnisskräfte vermehrt haben.","d":[101,118],"en":"The truths that we forget have in any case not been wholly useless, because they have increased the degree of our powers of cognition.","e":[114,133]}],"bewegungsgrund":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 238","link":"meier:meier-para-238.1","de":"Alsdenn enthält die gelehrte Erkenntniss Bewegungsgründe §.232; nicht nur sie selbst zu  begehren §.237, sondern auch ihren Gegenstand entweder zu begehren oder zu verabscheuen.","d":[41,56],"en":"Then the learned cognition contains motives §.232; not only to desire itself §.237, but also either to desire or to abhor its object.","e":[36,43]}],"verstandesgebrauch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:608","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-001.3","de":"Ohne das besondere ist der Verstandesgebrauch nur in einer gewißen Wißenschaft möglich.","d":[27,45],"en":"Without the particular, the use of the understanding is possible only in a certain science.","e":[28,52]}],"vernunftgebrauch":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:646","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-052.13","de":"Dieser Kritische Gebrauch der Vernunft ist bei den angeführten Arten des Vernunftgebrauchs zu empfehlen, weil er denn nur urtheilt, wenn man die Quellen genugsam examinirt hat.","d":[73,90],"en":"This critical use of reason is to be recommended among the kinds of use of reason mentioned, because he judges only when one has sufficiently examined the sources.","e":[14,27]}],"schlussurteil":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 357","link":"meier:meier-para-357.1","de":"Das Subject des Schlussurtheils, ist der kleinere Hauptbegriff (terminus minor), sein Prädicat aber, der grössere Hauptbegriff (terminus maior).","d":[16,31],"en":"The subject of the conclusion is the smaller principal concept (terminus minor), but its predicate the greater principal concept (terminus maior).","e":null}],"worterklaerung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 280","link":"meier:meier-para-280.1","de":"Jene ist eine Sacherklärung (definitio realis, genetica), diese aber eine Worterklärung (definitio nominalis).","d":[74,87],"en":"The former is a real definition (definitio realis, genetica), the latter however a nominal definition (definitio nominalis).","e":[83,101]}],"sacherklaerung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 280","link":"meier:meier-para-280.1","de":"Jene ist eine Sacherklärung (definitio realis, genetica), diese aber eine Worterklärung (definitio nominalis).","d":[14,27],"en":"The former is a real definition (definitio realis, genetica), the latter however a nominal definition (definitio nominalis).","e":[16,31]}],"undeutlichkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:137","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s07-304.1","de":"Wenn eine Sache gar zu viele Merckmahle hat, so, daß man dieselben auf einemahl zu übersehen nicht im Stande ist, so liegt nothwendig die Schuld von der Undeutlichkeit derselben an der Sache selbst.","d":[153,167],"en":"If a thing has far too many marks, so that one is not in a position to survey them all at once, the fault of its indistinctness necessarily lies in the thing itself.","e":[113,127]}],"unwahrheit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:89","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-090.0","de":"Die Unmöglichkeit aber ist im Gegentheil ein allemahl zureichender, und Sufficienter Grund zum untrüglichen Beweise der Unwahrheit, oder Falschheit einer Sache.","d":[120,130],"en":"Impossibility, however, is on the opposite side an always sufficient and Sufficient ground for the infallible proof of the untruth or falsity of a thing.","e":[123,130]}],"richtigkeit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:672","link":"busolt:busolt-s26-055.4","de":"Bey den Hypothetischen ist nur bloß das Verhältniß zweierley Urtheile, wie eins aus der Richtigkeit des andern folgt.","d":[88,99],"en":"In hypothetical ones there is merely the relation of two judgments, how one follows from the correctness of the other.","e":[93,104]}],"unrichtigkeit":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 94","link":"meier:meier-para-94.2","de":"Jene sind die innerlichen, und diese die äusserlichen Kennzeichen der Richtigkeit und Unrichtigkeit (criteria interna et externa veritatis et falsitatis cognitionis).","d":[86,99],"en":"The former are the internal, and the latter the external marks of correctness and incorrectness (criteria interna et externa veritatis et falsitatis cognitionis).","e":[82,95]}],"fehler":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:684","link":"busolt:busolt-s31-012.1","de":"Soll diese Künstliche keinen Fehler haben, so muß sie Natur seyn; denn die Kunst ist wirklich nichts anders als Kultivirte Natur.","d":[29,35],"en":"If this artificial method is to have no fault, it must be nature; for art is really nothing other than cultivated nature.","e":[40,45]}],"gedanke":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:47","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-045.2","de":"Das urbild aller Vollkommenheiten aber ist immer nur in Gedancken. es ist ein Archetypon, und blos ein Ideal.","d":[56,65],"en":"The archetype of all perfections, however, is always only in thought. It is an archetypon, and merely an ideal.","e":[61,68]}],"denken":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:614","link":"busolt:busolt-s04-005.14","de":"Unser Denken ist eigentlich ein Erkenntniß durch Begriffe, oder eine discursive Erkenntniß.","d":[6,12],"en":"Our thinking is properly a cognition through concepts, or a discursive cognition.","e":[4,12]}],"denkungsart":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:683","link":"busolt:busolt-s31-004.1","de":"Dies Tumultuarische in der Methode ist allemal ein Beweis von einer Tumultuarischen Denkungsart.","d":[84,95],"en":"This tumultuary in method is always a proof of a tumultuary way of thinking.","e":[60,75]}],"einsicht":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:93","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s06-122.0","de":"Man muß also der Bekanndtmachung der Urtheile, das ist der Aussetzung derselbigen, denen Einsichten aller keine Hinderniße entgegen setzen.","d":[89,99],"en":"One must therefore set no obstacles against the making known of judgments, that is, the putting forth of them, to the insights of all.","e":[118,126]}],"voraussetzung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:651","link":"busolt:busolt-s17-017.9","de":"Die nothwendige Voraussezzung einer Erkenntniß mit dem praktischen Interesse ist glauben.","d":[16,29],"en":"The necessary presupposition of a cognition with practical interest is believing.","e":[14,28]}],"beurteilung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:23","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-041.10","de":"So ist es auch mit der Arzney-Kunst. zur Beurtheilung der Sittlichkeit, des Rechts, und Unrechts hingegen ist keine Wißenschaft, und Gelahrtsamkeit vonnöthen.","d":[41,53],"en":"So it is also with the art of medicine. For judging morality, right and wrong, on the other hand, no science and erudition is needed.","e":[44,51]}],"anwendung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:656","link":"busolt:busolt-s19-019.0","de":"Vom Begriff in abstracto muß ich allmahlich zum Begriff in concreto hinabsteigen, weil sonst keine Anwendung ist.","d":[99,108],"en":"From the concept in abstracto I must gradually descend to the concept in concreto, because otherwise there is no application.","e":[113,124]}],"ausuebung":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:649","link":"busolt:busolt-s16-005.8","de":"Wenn er gleich nach einem Riß arbeitet, so ist er nur ein Copist, er hat aber eine Ausübung nach der Idee des andern, die er faßen können muß.","d":[83,91],"en":"Even if he works according to a plan, he is only a copyist; he has, however, an exercise according to the idea of another, which he must be able to grasp.","e":[80,88]}],"bedeutung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 452","link":"meier:meier-para-452.0","de":"Ein grober Ausdruck (terminus crassus) ist ein Ausdruck, dessen Bedeutung eine grobe Erkenntniss ist §.102.","d":[64,73],"en":"A coarse expression (terminus crassus) is an expression whose meaning is a coarse cognition §.102.","e":[62,69]}],"ausdruck":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:294","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s14-005.1","de":"Der Ausdruck heißt verständlich, der da kann verstanden werden. verständlich kann etwas seyn, ohne daß es deutlich sey.","d":[4,12],"en":"An expression is called intelligible that can be understood. Something can be intelligible without being distinct.","e":[3,13]}],"untersuchung":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:154","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-110.0","de":"Eine Erkenntniß aber ist ad Analogiam seicht, wenn sie sich auf bloße Erfahrungen und auf keiner Untersuchung gründet.","d":[97,109],"en":"But a cognition is shallow ad Analogiam when it is grounded on mere experiences and on no investigation.","e":[90,103]}],"einwurf":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:203","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s08-448.0","de":"Ausgemachte Wahrheiten sind diejenige Wahrheiten wieder welche ferner kein Einwurf gemacht werden kann.","d":[75,82],"en":"Established truths are those truths against which no further objection can be made.","e":[61,70]}],"aufloesung":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 328","link":"meier:meier-para-328.6","de":"Die Probe der Aufgabe (proba, examen problematis) ist dasjenige, wodurch man überzeugt wird, dass man die Auflösung beobachtet habe.","d":[106,115],"en":"The test of the problem (proba, examen problematis) is that by which one is convinced that one has observed the solution.","e":[112,120]}],"kunst":[{"t":"meier","cite":"§ 399","link":"meier:meier-para-399.1","de":"Um die logische Kunst zu verbergen, und die Pedanterei zu vermeiden, sind die versteckten Vernunftschlüsse anzupreisen.","d":[16,21],"en":"In order to conceal the logical art, and to avoid pedantry, hidden inferences of reason are to be recommended.","e":[32,35]}],"nutzen":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:39","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s02-091.2","de":"Eine Logica aber , die so dun ckel und übermäßig verfeineret ist, als des Crusii seine, kann diesen Nutzen nicht haben.","d":[100,106],"en":"A logic, however, that is as obscure and excessively refined as that of Crusius cannot have this utility.","e":[97,104]}],"lehre":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:611","link":"busolt:busolt-s02-011.3","de":"Die aesthetic ist die Lehre der Sinnlichen Urtheilskraft, ob ein Werk des Genies, oder sonst etwas gefällt, oder nicht.","d":[22,27],"en":"Aesthetic is the doctrine of the sensible power of judgment, whether a work of genius, or something else, pleases or not.","e":[17,25]}],"gewohnheit":[{"t":"busolt","cite":"AA 24:642","link":"busolt:busolt-s14-027.1","de":"Der Hang, der aus der neuen Gewohnheit entstanden ist, macht die Vorurtheile zur Nothwendigkeit.","d":[28,38],"en":"The propensity that has arisen from the new habit makes the prejudices into a necessity.","e":[44,49]}],"taetigkeit":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:45","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s03-033.2","de":"Das, was unser Leben begünstiget, d.i. was unsere Thätigkeit gleichsam ins Spiel sezet, das gefällt. es wird uns etwas leicht, wenn es in Ordnung ist.","d":[50,60],"en":"What favors our life, i.e. what, as it were, sets our activity into play, pleases. Something becomes easy for us when it is in order.","e":[54,62]}],"charakter":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:295","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s15-002.1","de":"Hier bedeutet es den Character seine Gedancken auszudrücken. jeder hat seinen besondern Styl, so wie jeder seine besondere Hand schreibet.","d":[21,30],"en":"Here it means the character of expressing one's thoughts. Everyone has his own particular style, just as everyone writes his own particular hand.","e":[18,27]}],"gemein":[{"t":"blomberg","cite":"AA 24:18","link":"blomberg:blomberg-s01-025.1","de":"Allein wenn keine andere Principia als die Erfahrungen sind . so bleibt eine gesunde Vernunft doch eine gemeine Vernunft.","d":[104,111],"en":"But if there are no other principia than experiences, a sound reason still remains a common reason.","e":[85,91]}]};
